WEBVTT

02:16.612 --> 02:18.404
We, we are ready to start the meeting.

02:24.130 --> 02:27.750
We, we are ready. We'll give a couple minutes to quiet down.

02:29.243 --> 02:32.367
Can you hear me okay, Lacey? Uh, yes, I can hear you.

02:33.342 --> 02:36.750
Okay, perfect. We'll go ahead and get started. Uh, before we call the

02:37.250 --> 02:40.448
meeting to order, I've asked Brett Wright, Council Member Wright, if he'd offer a prayer.

02:40.513 --> 02:43.777
So, uh, when it's quiet there, Brett, if you'd, uh, lead us out.

02:47.770 --> 02:50.742
Our Heavenly Father, we're grateful this evening to be able to bow our heads in

02:50.838 --> 02:53.827
prayer and express gratitude for the opportunity to gather as fellow,

02:54.229 --> 02:57.675
fellow citizens. We're grateful to live

02:58.175 --> 03:01.887
in this great city, in this great state and in the United

03:02.387 --> 03:06.365
States of America and to be able to enjoy the freedoms and opportunity

03:06.865 --> 03:09.800
to pursue life in the way that we choose.

03:10.619 --> 03:14.488
We express gratitude for the many blessings that we have, for the safety that we

03:14.988 --> 03:18.260
enjoy, for one another's camaraderie and companionship.

03:18.982 --> 03:22.578
We pray, Father, as we're about to embark in several

03:23.078 --> 03:26.575
hours of discussion and opportunity to listen, we pray that thou bless us with listening

03:26.687 --> 03:29.914
ears and listening hearts. Bless us with those

03:30.414 --> 03:33.527
of us who will speak, those of us who have come with an opportunity to

03:33.736 --> 03:37.252
express comment and thoughts and,

03:38.393 --> 03:41.845
and with a desire to help the city council hear the

03:42.345 --> 03:46.164
concerns that they may want to raise. Bless those

03:46.180 --> 03:49.360
that will speak with the ability to articulate their words,

03:50.468 --> 03:53.952
to be able to do so in the allotted time. Bless us with civility

03:54.145 --> 03:57.512
one to another. Bless us to be

03:58.012 --> 04:01.461
appropriate in our actions, to maintain at all times

04:01.494 --> 04:05.313
the decorum that is expected in this public setting.

04:06.009 --> 04:09.478
We express gratitude for our employees, for our first responders,

04:10.240 --> 04:13.889
for those who are serving in the military. We pray that we'll be mindful of

04:14.389 --> 04:17.971
them and their families. Bless us to be aware of those who are

04:18.471 --> 04:21.197
less fortunate than us, those who are in need.

04:21.600 --> 04:24.471
Help us to continue to be the great neighbors that Eagle Mountain is known for.

04:24.600 --> 04:25.955
And these things we humbly pray in the name of Jesus Christ, amen. Amen.

04:31.723 --> 04:32.351
Amen. Okay,

04:36.444 --> 04:39.776
thank you, Brett. I appreciate it. Um, it is 6:02,

04:39.840 --> 04:43.777
and we'll officially call this meeting to order and, uh, ask that

04:44.277 --> 04:47.552
everybody stand and join Craig, who's going to lead us in the— Councilor Whiting will

04:48.052 --> 04:51.137
lead us in the Pledge of Allegiance. Yeah, if you could join me in the

04:51.637 --> 04:51.821
Pledge of Allegiance.

05:15.186 --> 05:18.499
Okay, thanks, Councilmember Whiting. Uh, just to start

05:18.999 --> 05:21.893
off, a couple of housekeeping items. First of all, I appreciate everybody accommodating me being

05:21.926 --> 05:25.573
remote. Uh, I can see a full house there,

05:26.026 --> 05:30.135
and I appreciate everybody showing up. We love it when people participate and,

05:30.232 --> 05:34.065
uh, come to the, to the meetings to help us

05:35.019 --> 05:37.638
make these difficult decisions for our city. Uh,

05:39.172 --> 05:42.393
I love technology and the fact that we're able to still join.

05:42.506 --> 05:45.030
I see there's quite a few participants online as well.

05:45.662 --> 05:49.374
Mayor, we're having a hard time hearing you. If you could speak right into the

05:49.874 --> 05:53.155
mic, it would be greatly appreciated. Okay, is that

05:53.655 --> 05:56.802
better? Yes,

05:56.818 --> 06:00.230
thank you. Okay. Yes, we appreciate you guys

06:00.730 --> 06:04.191
being there, and I'm sad that I'm not there in person due to a

06:04.595 --> 06:08.035
previous obligation, but I appreciate the fact that we can still join remote

06:08.535 --> 06:11.221
and have these same conversations. So,

06:11.708 --> 06:15.650
with that, we'll start. I saw— it looked like Natalie was passing out

06:15.780 --> 06:19.633
some packets. There are packets at the back of the room

06:19.697 --> 06:22.782
with the following documents available, just for public knowledge.

06:23.634 --> 06:27.507
It is the property tax impact schedule form from

06:28.007 --> 06:31.572
Eagle Mountain City. Also, a physical copy

06:31.604 --> 06:34.641
of the Utah County Notice of Proposed Tax Increase is

06:35.141 --> 06:38.755
available for review. The agenda is in that packet

06:39.255 --> 06:42.515
as well, and the Truth in Taxation overview or basics.

06:42.660 --> 06:47.080
And also, for more information, you can visit em.gov

06:47.580 --> 06:51.200
for— or eaglemountain.gov for additional information on

06:51.700 --> 06:54.900
our website. I know our communications team's kept that up, and it's, uh,

06:55.400 --> 06:59.260
it's been very good. So any other information that you're

06:59.760 --> 07:02.320
looking for, hopefully those are the areas you can find it. And if you need

07:02.820 --> 07:05.900
a packet, it's at the back of the room. Um,

07:06.400 --> 07:10.080
we're going to start with the agenda item 3A, which is the public hearing

07:10.580 --> 07:14.060
for proposed Property tax increase. Uh, there will be some rules,

07:14.110 --> 07:17.370
just like as our, uh, other meetings, some decorum.

07:17.870 --> 07:21.050
As was mentioned before, we expect everybody to be respectful and to

07:21.550 --> 07:24.830
follow the rules and, uh, make sure we handle this

07:25.330 --> 07:28.570
with respect. This public hearing is for the proposed property

07:29.070 --> 07:32.590
tax increase. Please keep your comments related to this topic

07:33.090 --> 07:36.870
only. The council will listen to all comments but will not engage

07:37.370 --> 07:41.158
in a discussion until the public hearing has been closed. Each person will

07:41.658 --> 07:43.418
have 3 minutes to address the council.

07:46.570 --> 07:49.326
We ask that everyone remain respectful throughout the hearing.

07:49.586 --> 07:52.731
Disruptive behavior, personal attacks, cheering,

07:53.153 --> 07:55.620
booing, clapping are not permitted.

07:56.644 --> 07:59.438
If this occurs, we'll— you'll be asked to leave the room.

08:01.038 --> 08:04.644
If you've submitted a public comment form online, Lacey will read your name.

08:05.796 --> 08:08.168
To see if you're in attendance to give your comments.

08:09.168 --> 08:13.121
After all comments are submitted, the meeting— in

08:13.621 --> 08:17.095
the meeting have been addressed, we will invite those attending in person to speak first,

08:17.564 --> 08:21.510
followed by those participating online. So Lacey will help us manage

08:21.543 --> 08:24.565
that. Everyone will have a chance to speak if you so desire.

08:25.561 --> 08:29.660
And we'll go in the order that she sets forth with people in

08:29.676 --> 08:33.019
person, the ones submitted online, and then those online.

08:33.928 --> 08:37.167
For those attending virtually, including email,

08:37.248 --> 08:39.918
by the way, for those attending virtually, when the time comes,

08:40.770 --> 08:44.735
uh, Lacey will call your name and will electronically ask you to unmute your microphone.

08:45.415 --> 08:48.361
Your 3-minute speaking time will begin once you start speaking.

08:49.635 --> 08:53.277
You're welcome to remain in the meeting to observe, but you will not be able

08:53.777 --> 08:56.724
to provide additional comment. Everybody gets one chance.

08:57.485 --> 09:01.351
If you prefer, you may continue watching the meeting through the city's

09:01.432 --> 09:04.830
online streaming portal. Please make sure to speak clearly

09:05.330 --> 09:09.060
into the microphone. After all speakers have had the opportunity to comment,

09:09.510 --> 09:12.850
the recorder's office will conduct one final check. We'll check

09:13.350 --> 09:15.870
to make sure everybody's had a chance. If you still feel like you haven't had

09:16.370 --> 09:19.410
a chance to speak, we'll allow one last chance and then we'll close the public

09:19.910 --> 09:23.790
hearing. So, I've read those things again. Order of events,

09:24.290 --> 09:27.430
we're going to start with public comment prior to the meeting, then the participants in

09:27.930 --> 09:30.728
attendance, then the virtual ones. Then email.

09:31.211 --> 09:34.673
Lacey, have you, uh, heard those instructions and do you feel like

09:35.173 --> 09:38.796
there's any clarification needed? I think you hit everything perfectly.

09:39.021 --> 09:41.742
We will go with it as we go, so we're good.

09:42.810 --> 09:47.086
Okay, perfectly. It is 5:07 on the 6th of

09:47.588 --> 09:50.733
August. Correct. Hang on, Mayor. Hang on, Mayor.

09:51.398 --> 09:54.834
Uh, you're in a different time zone. It's— I'm— yeah,

09:54.851 --> 09:57.774
6:07. 6:07, sorry.

09:58.352 --> 10:02.032
At, uh, I look at my clock and that's what told me. So 6:07 on

10:02.289 --> 10:06.002
August 6th, um, and we will now open this

10:06.502 --> 10:10.429
public hearing. So Lacey, I'll turn it to you to call up in order.

10:11.315 --> 10:13.827
Sounds great. We will go ahead and start with John Breeding.

10:21.777 --> 10:26.599
So I went online earlier today and I looked up that since

10:27.099 --> 10:30.944
2020 we've had about a 78% increase in revenues.

10:31.940 --> 10:34.000
We've had a population growth of about 60%.

10:35.299 --> 10:37.781
Inflation's run about 29% since then.

10:42.093 --> 10:46.167
And an 11% increase in taxes would give

10:46.215 --> 10:49.756
an inflation-adjusted equivalent of what

10:50.278 --> 10:51.719
we had for revenue in 2020.

10:52.951 --> 10:57.001
I'm kind of cynical. I believe that a 220%

10:58.232 --> 11:01.632
increase is kind of a head fake

11:01.697 --> 11:04.936
that I don't think anybody here actually believes that

11:05.436 --> 11:06.701
that's what is going to happen.

11:10.174 --> 11:14.049
But when you eventually come up with about a 40%

11:14.163 --> 11:17.827
increase in taxes, which is also outrageous,

11:18.781 --> 11:22.458
people will be less up in arms about it. And I

11:22.958 --> 11:26.554
don't understand why, as government, as our population

11:27.054 --> 11:30.785
grows and as the government grows, that you don't become more efficient

11:31.220 --> 11:34.305
with artificial intelligence and

11:34.354 --> 11:38.259
computers and things like that. It seems like government is the only

11:38.291 --> 11:41.243
thing that doesn't become more efficient with scale.

11:41.832 --> 11:43.011
Anyway, that's my comment.

11:46.707 --> 11:47.608
Chaz Roberts.

11:53.622 --> 11:56.684
I do not see Chaz Roberts in attendance. We will include it into the record.

11:57.457 --> 11:58.281
Melissa Bradley.

12:09.946 --> 12:13.251
I'm disappointed. I'm frustrated. It's not the resident's

12:13.751 --> 12:17.454
job to prevent a tax increase. Mayor, council,

12:17.566 --> 12:20.871
you're supposed to be able to prioritize needs over wants.

12:21.432 --> 12:24.801
I'm against the 220% property tax increase because

12:25.301 --> 12:29.052
it's not for public safety. It's for nonessential projects

12:29.552 --> 12:33.415
that the city can't afford. Let me be clear. I support funding our sheriff's office.

12:33.544 --> 12:37.073
I support paying employees competitive wages. I support needing roads,

12:37.137 --> 12:40.778
water, and sewer improvements, and you already have the money in place do all

12:41.278 --> 12:44.292
of that. This increase is a burden on the average taxpayer.

12:45.238 --> 12:49.105
25.2 million Americans under 35 lived with their

12:49.605 --> 12:52.843
parents last year. That's not normal. And raising our property

12:52.875 --> 12:56.308
taxes is not the solution. You're adding to this crisis.

12:56.725 --> 13:00.190
Craig, Rich, Brett, you all are real estate agents.

13:00.254 --> 13:04.024
You should understand this. Jared, you were the real estate agent. You should

13:04.524 --> 13:07.939
know the consequences. Zach, as an investor, you should get this. Melissa, as a mom

13:08.439 --> 13:11.935
with adults living in your home, I assume you understand. Thank you. Property tax increases

13:12.048 --> 13:15.500
don't stop with homeowners. Landlords will pass those costs

13:16.000 --> 13:19.756
to their renters, and our children and your residents will pay higher rent.

13:19.853 --> 13:22.695
Families will have less money to help their kids with rent,

13:22.888 --> 13:26.068
gasoline, or groceries. As housing costs rise,

13:26.261 --> 13:30.548
which they are unaffordable right now, young adults will stay home longer,

13:30.597 --> 13:34.098
and that delays their independence. Families already caring

13:34.194 --> 13:37.567
for adults, children, grandchildren, or aging parents have

13:38.067 --> 13:41.803
even less room in their budgets when you increase fixed housing

13:41.979 --> 13:45.169
costs. By increasing our property taxes, each one of

13:45.201 --> 13:48.679
you is choosing to negatively impact 26 families in

13:48.792 --> 13:52.062
my neighborhood. In one week, that will be 27 because

13:52.110 --> 13:54.626
my kids are moving in— my adult kids, 2 of them.

13:55.925 --> 13:59.467
When you're proposing what you're proposing is wrong, it's dishonest. When you

13:59.531 --> 14:03.170
claim it's for public safety, it isn't. It's for completely optional

14:03.670 --> 14:07.017
structures like a new city hall and rec center. And the fact that you had

14:07.065 --> 14:10.471
the city manager admit that on Tuesday instead of standing up

14:10.971 --> 14:14.600
and saying it for yourselves is crap. I hope you choose

14:14.616 --> 14:17.829
to lead with honesty moving forward. When you took your oath of

14:17.909 --> 14:21.572
office, you all promised to be faithful stewards of the taxpayer dollar.

14:22.167 --> 14:25.573
The people of Eagle Mountain work hard for each dollar they earn, and they're

14:26.073 --> 14:29.107
making difficult financial decisions every day. We want you

14:29.332 --> 14:32.690
to do the same. We have

14:33.190 --> 14:36.443
contracts in place. And they will benefit our community soon.

14:36.796 --> 14:40.466
Be patient. Focus on public safety, sewer, water,

14:40.546 --> 14:43.703
and roads. 30 seconds remaining. Stop looking to the taxpayers to

14:44.203 --> 14:47.148
solve your pretend budget crisis. We don't believe you.

14:47.677 --> 14:51.347
Go attract businesses to expand the tax business, and you— and

14:51.379 --> 14:55.193
then you better leave residents' sales tax alone.

14:56.186 --> 15:00.181
I caught that in Tuesday's meeting. It is our right to decide When and how

15:00.681 --> 15:03.717
we want to spend our money. Stay out of our pockets. Our community wants freedom

15:03.749 --> 15:07.672
from taxes, not slavery to it. Do not raise property taxes and no new

15:07.785 --> 15:08.318
taxes.

15:21.637 --> 15:24.894
I'm just going to remind you that the mayor gave us clear instructions that we're

15:25.394 --> 15:28.681
not going to entertain that. Clapping was not part of those

15:28.730 --> 15:32.015
instructions. Yes, it was. So we're going to ask

15:32.515 --> 15:37.059
you to refrain from that type of outburst because it's going to delay the opportunity

15:37.091 --> 15:41.155
for those who want to come and speak to us. So please refrain

15:41.268 --> 15:45.139
from that, or according to his instructions, we're going to ask you

15:50.028 --> 15:53.349
I do have Adam Brady for the next one. It does say

15:53.592 --> 15:56.663
my wife Melissa will read the statement. I am unsure if he's here. Adam Bradley.

16:00.819 --> 16:03.866
Sorry, you have to hear from me again. Good evening, Mayor and Council. My name

16:04.366 --> 16:07.634
is Adam Bradley, and I'm here to strongly oppose this proposed 220%

16:08.070 --> 16:11.855
property tax increase. In fact, I believe you should be lowering taxes and

16:12.355 --> 16:15.711
not raising them. A 220% increase is an enormous

16:15.791 --> 16:19.181
ask. Saying it's justified simply because property taxes

16:19.245 --> 16:22.592
haven't been raised in 15 years is an insult to basic math.

16:23.267 --> 16:27.104
This represents real money for families already struggling with inflation,

16:27.377 --> 16:30.524
rising home values, and higher taxes across the board.

16:31.294 --> 16:35.019
Eagle Mountain's explosive growth has already expanded the city's revenue

16:35.163 --> 16:39.129
through impact fees, building permits, and commercial development. So why

16:39.193 --> 16:42.757
isn't that growing paying for these needs? I've seen

16:42.805 --> 16:46.802
no convincing evidence that existing revenue can't fund competitive

16:47.302 --> 16:51.169
wages for our employees, and I've seen no categorical proof that we need

16:51.217 --> 16:55.785
more sheriff deputies. Comparing Eagle Mountain to other cities doesn't

16:55.801 --> 16:58.662
work. There's no other city like Eagle Mountain.

16:59.410 --> 17:02.848
Show me the 911 calls that aren't being answered. Show me domestic

17:02.913 --> 17:06.432
violence calls going unanswered. Show me crimes not being

17:06.529 --> 17:09.999
solved. I haven't seen that evidence. Until a few days ago,

17:10.176 --> 17:13.823
residents were told every dollar of this tax increase would go to public

17:14.323 --> 17:18.068
safety. Then people started doing the math. The sheriff's contract increases

17:18.116 --> 17:21.557
by roughly $1.5 million while this tax hike brings in

17:21.605 --> 17:22.385
about $6.7 million. Order.

17:24.658 --> 17:28.088
Only after residents started asking questions did you admit the

17:28.185 --> 17:31.247
rest is for other projects, including a new city hall.

17:31.872 --> 17:34.180
This was never just about public safety.

17:34.854 --> 17:37.547
I've also heard almost no discussion of alternatives.

17:38.060 --> 17:41.426
Where's the debate? Where are the compromises? One council

17:41.926 --> 17:44.841
member even told my wife to do the research and come back with ideas.

17:45.595 --> 17:48.817
With respect, that's the job that you were elected to do.

17:49.764 --> 17:53.153
When I served on this council, I said no all the time because

17:53.201 --> 17:57.039
protecting taxpayers came first. Growth should be allowing

17:57.136 --> 18:00.412
us to reduce the tax burden, not asking

18:00.509 --> 18:04.443
families to pay more. I'll leave you with this: Have

18:04.943 --> 18:08.925
you forgotten the proper role of city government? This council and

18:08.957 --> 18:12.297
the last have continued to grow government and spending.

18:12.731 --> 18:17.357
What happened to Eagle Mountain being a place that

18:17.857 --> 18:21.089
that valued limited government and respected taxpayers. Please, no more.

18:22.590 --> 18:25.813
Please vote no on this increase and start looking for ways

18:25.846 --> 18:29.456
to lower our property tax instead. And on a personal note,

18:29.633 --> 18:30.455
I would like to add,

18:33.206 --> 18:36.826
I love Adam. 30 seconds remaining. He was a great council member,

18:37.731 --> 18:39.088
and he worked hard.

18:41.780 --> 18:44.076
You're, you're reading his statement, not your own.

18:46.060 --> 18:46.788
You don't get to go twice.

18:52.540 --> 18:53.117
Ben Bracknell.

18:56.913 --> 19:00.127
I don't see Ben Bracknell. Um, it says opposition to proposed

19:00.627 --> 19:04.193
tax increase. Um, I do want to remind those of you online,

19:04.450 --> 19:08.020
uh, for the Zoom link, this is for participating virtually. If you want to watch

19:08.135 --> 19:10.753
the meeting and not participate, you can go to our portal to watch it.

19:11.156 --> 19:14.386
I do have Alex Washburn, uh, for the public comment, but I do see

19:14.886 --> 19:17.179
you're online, so we will call you when the virtual time comes.

19:18.308 --> 19:20.590
Um, Ashley Lauer, or Lower,

19:23.530 --> 19:26.792
um, it only says property tax increase. I do not

19:26.841 --> 19:30.849
see her, but we will add it to the record. Duncan Searcy.

19:35.101 --> 19:38.192
Sorry, I didn't hear the mayor say no clapping. He was quiet,

19:39.010 --> 19:43.407
but I also don't think our First Amendment rights care much about his decorum.

19:43.744 --> 19:47.981
So the title of this meeting is Truth in Taxation

19:48.495 --> 19:51.865
Public Hearing. I want to quote the city. This is what

19:52.365 --> 19:55.700
they said. Eagle Mountain City is proposing a property

19:56.200 --> 19:59.295
tax increase with every dollar going straight to public safety,

19:59.488 --> 20:02.954
period. So that's a lie, and we all

20:03.454 --> 20:06.146
know that now. And so that's not a great way to start this meeting off.

20:06.226 --> 20:09.610
I was a lot nicer on Tuesday when I spoke, but some of the

20:10.110 --> 20:12.626
responses I got from you actually is what made me upset, and I'm not gonna

20:13.126 --> 20:16.234
be quite as nice tonight. You'll see some of the pensioners I mentioned on Tuesday

20:16.734 --> 20:20.356
are here. That's great. Every single one of you, when I brought this up,

20:20.404 --> 20:24.012
expressed remorse, like, we don't wanna be doing this, you know?

20:24.333 --> 20:27.685
This is so hard on our community. This is just a necessary

20:27.701 --> 20:30.957
evil that we have to do. And Brett, you said something

20:31.005 --> 20:34.620
that struck me. You said, we have been called upon. To make this

20:35.120 --> 20:39.115
decision. Brett, who is calling upon you to raise the property taxes

20:39.617 --> 20:42.964
if we elect you and you work for us? I would like to

20:43.012 --> 20:46.262
know after all this is done if you would address that specifically.

20:46.650 --> 20:49.738
Who's calling upon you to make any kind of decision? Okay.

20:50.450 --> 20:53.935
And then Melissa, it bothered you so much, just the thought of raising taxes

20:54.035 --> 20:55.877
on our poor families brought you to tears.

20:57.625 --> 21:00.827
Sweetheart, you don't need to be upset. Just vote no. You don't have to raise

21:00.925 --> 21:03.768
the taxes. This is your choice. you get to vote yes or no.

21:04.585 --> 21:08.128
Okay? So I think we

21:08.628 --> 21:12.409
just need to realize everybody is struggling in this economy,

21:12.665 --> 21:16.465
every single person. Okay? If we as citizens are

21:16.513 --> 21:19.671
tightening our belts and we're deciding what we have to cut out

21:20.171 --> 21:23.727
of our lives, so must the city. Okay? There's money coming

21:24.227 --> 21:27.719
down the pipeline. Mayor Gray preaches about it all the time. So let's—

21:27.735 --> 21:30.801
Thank you. Tighten up our belt as a city instead

21:31.301 --> 21:34.977
of pushing those tax burdens onto the regular person. Okay.

21:35.699 --> 21:39.521
And Melissa, I'm sorry, I'm going to call you out a little bit. I'm tired

21:39.570 --> 21:42.974
of the performative testimony meeting style emotion.

21:43.327 --> 21:46.764
It's manipulative. Okay. And you have the chance tonight

21:47.264 --> 21:49.944
to vote no and prove that I'm wrong and that you really do care about

21:49.992 --> 21:53.975
the poor families. But when you sit up there and get emotional, it really bothers

21:54.007 --> 21:58.005
those of us that have discernment. Okay? A big reason

21:58.505 --> 22:01.932
why we're here tonight is because you gave Meta, a $1.5 trillion

22:02.206 --> 22:05.173
company, a 20-year tax break. Okay?

22:06.206 --> 22:09.239
Had you not done that— 30 seconds remaining. I don't think we'd be in this

22:09.287 --> 22:13.385
financial situation that we're at. And you keep touting this infrastructure

22:13.724 --> 22:16.769
that Facebook has brought to the city. I have never once driven out to the

22:17.269 --> 22:21.101
Facebook building, probably never will. They have not improved anything

22:21.117 --> 22:23.935
in the city that we, the citizens, use on a daily basis.

22:24.867 --> 22:28.078
So stop trying to gaslight us into like, oh,

22:28.094 --> 22:31.563
Facebook has been such a good deal, this is such a good deal. We're tired

22:32.063 --> 22:35.545
of it. Start working for us, or next election we

22:35.625 --> 22:39.077
are going to speak even louder. Your time is up.

22:39.318 --> 22:39.671
Thank you.

22:53.922 --> 22:58.077
Ryan Parker also

22:58.577 --> 23:00.853
does not say— just says property tax increase. I do not see him here,

23:00.934 --> 23:03.330
so we'll add it to the record. Charles Peterson.

23:07.081 --> 23:10.363
Good evening. As a former federal government

23:10.573 --> 23:13.778
program analyst, I have more questions than answers.

23:13.989 --> 23:16.857
So in reviewing all this material,

23:17.686 --> 23:19.759
What I'll give you is some questions.

23:20.820 --> 23:25.014
We've moved here— well, we've been here for 10 years now and so

23:25.514 --> 23:28.838
on. So I've got a number of questions that bother me. A couple of

23:29.338 --> 23:35.305
these things have already been mentioned. Of the $6.9

23:35.337 --> 23:38.783
million, and with $1.5

23:38.800 --> 23:42.687
million for the added police officers,

23:43.665 --> 23:47.566
I would be curious what the analysis was done— sorry,

23:47.647 --> 23:51.079
as an analyst— to say how

23:51.127 --> 23:54.366
do we need that many more? And it's already

23:54.398 --> 23:58.863
been addressed a little bit. Is our

23:58.976 --> 24:02.262
public safety been reduced without these?

24:03.363 --> 24:06.659
I don't know. That's a question that I have.

24:08.646 --> 24:14.421
Second— is

24:14.502 --> 24:18.211
looking at the information that was available, by going and approving

24:18.243 --> 24:22.093
this, we will become the most— I think the second most

24:23.822 --> 24:27.829
property taxed city in Jefferson— I'm sorry,

24:30.290 --> 24:34.255
I'm thinking of my own old county, but in Utah County,

24:34.934 --> 24:39.083
we are now second best. And I was reading

24:39.583 --> 24:43.191
a piece talking about being so wonderful about

24:43.691 --> 24:47.229
how our taxes are low. Now, if this

24:47.729 --> 24:49.638
is approved, we're going to go right up to the top. Excuse me.

24:51.514 --> 24:56.092
The other thing that bothers me as an analyst is

24:56.189 --> 24:58.503
the other— what is it?

25:00.655 --> 25:04.854
About 5. Yeah, 5.4 million goes into

25:05.323 --> 25:08.361
public safety. Now,

25:10.025 --> 25:12.576
is there a fund called public safety?

25:13.736 --> 25:17.410
What happens to that? Is there an outline of all

25:17.443 --> 25:21.104
the things that you're going to do with this $5.4

25:21.298 --> 25:24.824
million? I haven't

25:25.324 --> 25:25.406
seen anything.

25:28.608 --> 25:31.800
So what we would expect as an analyst is to say, okay,

25:32.904 --> 25:35.256
and I've had a lot of dealings with budget analysts.

25:36.125 --> 25:40.779
What are we actually talking about? What are the line items and

25:40.860 --> 25:44.657
what are those results going to be? 30 seconds remaining. I think that's

25:45.157 --> 25:48.959
critical. And if you can't show that, then we ought not to be

25:49.201 --> 25:51.565
voting for it, frankly. Thank you very much.

25:57.813 --> 26:00.833
I do want to clarify that we We do have Ryan Parker online, so we'll

26:01.333 --> 26:05.521
go back to his comment, but he is virtual. Dave Bresheenahan.

26:08.055 --> 26:08.539
Thank you.

26:13.682 --> 26:16.870
Mr. Mayor and City Council, thank you for allowing me the opportunity

26:16.903 --> 26:20.236
to speak. I'm grateful for each

26:20.364 --> 26:24.317
one of you, and I know how tough your job is. I really

26:24.387 --> 26:26.977
do. I wouldn't want to be in your position.

26:28.892 --> 26:32.249
The people that you represent, the people of Eagle Mountain,

26:33.492 --> 26:35.623
which has a median age of 23,

26:37.176 --> 26:40.412
and approximately 44% of our

26:40.912 --> 26:43.198
population are under 18,

26:44.342 --> 26:47.625
which helps us to see this is a community filled with

26:47.675 --> 26:49.397
a lot of young families.

26:52.509 --> 26:55.489
Then there's people over 65, like me.

26:56.531 --> 27:00.345
We only make up about 3% of Eagle Mountain. Young families

27:00.457 --> 27:04.927
are just getting started building careers and do not have a significant

27:05.427 --> 27:11.241
income, with the median individual income of $48,105

27:11.417 --> 27:14.862
per person. The average retired couple

27:15.343 --> 27:19.680
have a combined income of $79,315.

27:21.315 --> 27:23.937
We are all strapped for cash.

27:25.266 --> 27:28.823
The cost of living is making it harder and harder for the

27:28.903 --> 27:33.181
average family to get by. The added proposed tax

27:33.569 --> 27:37.131
adds to that burden and makes life more difficult than it already

27:37.293 --> 27:41.087
is for the vast majority of all these young families.

27:42.733 --> 27:44.444
I got my numbers from Google, by the way.

27:46.171 --> 27:50.108
Eagle Mountain charges an impact fee on new residential and

27:50.140 --> 27:54.448
commercial development. That fee is intended

27:54.674 --> 27:58.210
to fund the expansion of services because of the

27:58.307 --> 27:59.914
impact of that development.

28:01.996 --> 28:05.243
A portion of that impact fee is intended for public safety.

28:07.520 --> 28:10.712
I know about impact fees because I was a

28:10.744 --> 28:14.282
member of the legislature when we voted that into state

28:14.347 --> 28:16.677
law. I go back a ways.

28:19.470 --> 28:23.220
Families, young and old, have a specific income that must be

28:23.301 --> 28:26.178
budgeted to take care of all the expenses for their family.

28:27.127 --> 28:30.412
As the cost of living goes up, families must find ways

28:30.525 --> 28:34.987
to cut corners and tighten the budget, which means shopping

28:35.068 --> 28:38.575
sales, using coupons, using Facebook Marketplace,

28:39.208 --> 28:42.848
and they do without A lot of times in

28:42.896 --> 28:46.296
order to make it all work. 30 seconds remaining. I would suggest

28:46.344 --> 28:49.920
that the city has the mechanism to pay for additional services

28:50.353 --> 28:53.367
that come with the growth of the city through impact fees.

28:54.041 --> 28:56.655
I know developers hate those fees,

28:57.489 --> 29:00.808
but it's a part of the cost of doing business.

29:01.722 --> 29:05.843
And they are making millions in Eagle Mountain. Those impact

29:05.891 --> 29:09.167
fees won't affect their millions. Hopefully,

29:09.313 --> 29:13.341
the city can find ways to become more efficient in the services

29:13.374 --> 29:16.842
that the city provides. I ask the city council to— Your

29:17.342 --> 29:18.067
time is up. Thank you.

29:27.795 --> 29:28.458
Brian Free.

29:34.164 --> 29:36.474
Great to be here today. I want to thank you all for not kicking the

29:36.974 --> 29:40.356
can down the road. Uh, seems like the trend since I've lived here

29:40.421 --> 29:43.918
for 20, 20 years. The can keeps getting kicked down the road so we can

29:43.934 --> 29:47.207
keep our taxes low or whatever, and the needs of our city

29:47.223 --> 29:49.693
continue to grow. We're a growing city. There's needs and they have to be taken

29:49.709 --> 29:52.629
care of. So thank you for that. Um, I, I think that goes a note.

29:52.758 --> 29:55.597
I, I also want to say that a lot of us have probably had a

29:56.097 --> 29:59.657
knee-jerk reaction to, to a 220% increase,

29:59.673 --> 30:04.493
which is actually lower if you add in, you know, your fire and your sheriffs

30:04.993 --> 30:06.774
and put that all together like another city would have in their city tax.

30:06.822 --> 30:09.056
We're probably right in the middle, and then we're probably at the top when we

30:09.072 --> 30:13.201
add 220%. So that's, you know, so that's more of an apples-to-apples comparison,

30:13.233 --> 30:16.302
which is good to do. I think one of the issues is there wasn't a

30:16.802 --> 30:19.869
lot of transparency, right? So we're not seeing what you guys are seeing, and that

30:19.997 --> 30:24.416
may not necessarily be right on you, but on those who were tasked

30:24.916 --> 30:28.014
with putting out information for us. Um, we like to see what all those— we

30:28.514 --> 30:31.660
like to know that it's not 100% for one thing, one portion, that it's for

30:31.708 --> 30:34.502
a bunch of things that are all needs within our city. And, and seeing those

30:34.599 --> 30:37.345
line items is really helpful so we can see exactly what it's paid for.

30:37.490 --> 30:39.562
There may be a lot of us that would say I don't like it,

30:40.236 --> 30:42.886
but those are all needs. I don't know how we don't take care of them.

30:42.967 --> 30:45.617
And if we saw what each of those things are, right, and maybe we'd have

30:46.117 --> 30:50.001
some different, different type of discussion because we would all come more informed without

30:50.017 --> 30:53.163
having to dig deep to try to find those answers. On our own and do

30:53.663 --> 30:56.994
that work that could easily be provided for us because you guys already

30:57.494 --> 30:59.896
have it, some of that information. So that would be very helpful for us to

31:00.396 --> 31:04.271
see what those line items are. I will say that in

31:04.368 --> 31:07.397
addition, one of the things that we want to make sure we're doing is that

31:07.429 --> 31:11.276
we're taking advantage of looking at the things that, let's say my basement's

31:11.776 --> 31:13.793
flooding, I got to get that water shut off and get that water out of

31:14.293 --> 31:16.598
there and clean everything up or I'm going to lose my home, right? Those are

31:17.098 --> 31:18.409
the kind of things we need to take care of. And I know we have

31:18.909 --> 31:21.924
some of those kinds of issues. In our city that need to be addressed that

31:22.424 --> 31:24.688
maybe we don't always see day to day as residents. And so that's important.

31:25.218 --> 31:29.202
Um, but 220% or the lower number, if we include everything together,

31:29.475 --> 31:32.367
whatever that percent is, it's still an increase. It's still a tax,

31:32.849 --> 31:36.175
um, with everything else like has been mentioned that, that we're seeing increase in

31:36.675 --> 31:39.822
our lives. And we want to make sure that that's being— um, we're looking

31:39.838 --> 31:43.613
at zero. Let's say we can't do anything, zero, without going into major

31:44.113 --> 31:46.409
debt to do it. And then add to that, well, what can we do?

31:46.762 --> 31:49.790
And then what can we do in 2, 3 years when some of that data

31:50.290 --> 31:53.347
center money starts coming off? Like, when they first were talking about data centers,

31:53.379 --> 31:56.263
we were told whatever the size is, one data center is like 4 or 5

31:56.296 --> 31:59.196
Costcos or Walmarts worth of revenue. That's a lot of revenue.

31:59.676 --> 32:01.888
If that starts coming on board in a couple years, we've got a lot of

32:02.388 --> 32:04.195
revenue coming our way, right? So we'll be able to— we should be able to

32:04.708 --> 32:08.217
then reduce taxes. 30 seconds remaining. But one thing I'll leave you with,

32:08.393 --> 32:12.111
just because it's a buzz term, let's not

32:12.611 --> 32:16.026
California our Utah. A 220% increase is

32:16.526 --> 32:19.370
a California in our Utah. And that's something I don't think any of you want

32:19.870 --> 32:22.730
to do or any of you are in favor of. Most of you would consider

32:23.230 --> 32:27.084
yourself conservative, fiscally conservative, and I would hope that you'll really take that into consideration.

32:27.181 --> 32:31.282
Thank you. Matt Oakman.

32:33.905 --> 32:36.642
I don't see him online and I don't see him in person. We'll add him

32:36.658 --> 32:39.184
to the record. Matthew Endicott.

32:49.165 --> 32:51.857
My name is Matt Endicott, and I've lived in Eagle Mountain for about 6 years.

32:52.530 --> 32:55.943
I've listened to the presentation given by Chief Deputy Knutson in April, as well as

32:55.975 --> 32:59.404
the comments I've received from the city council in response to my email this week.

32:59.965 --> 33:02.978
Um, thank you for your responses. Um, but I seem to have missed some important

33:03.250 --> 33:06.663
discussion in Tuesday's meeting. Um, I'll have to go back and review that.

33:06.936 --> 33:09.934
After reviewing of the budget that was released earlier this week, this issue has been

33:10.560 --> 33:13.670
made clear. The messaging from the mayor was confusing and may have led to the

33:14.170 --> 33:17.872
level of negative responses being voiced, but after review, I have a couple of questions.

33:18.256 --> 33:21.544
Based on my review, the proposed public safety budget is about $10 million,

33:21.945 --> 33:24.767
which is, you know, based off of other things, which is about $2 million higher

33:24.831 --> 33:28.102
than last year. This revenue from property taxes

33:28.118 --> 33:31.646
last year covered about 50% of the previous costs,

33:32.127 --> 33:35.640
with the other 50% coming from the general fund. So sales tax or

33:36.140 --> 33:39.317
other things, if I understand that correctly. So I have a couple questions. Why is

33:39.349 --> 33:43.187
it necessary for the entire amount of the sheriff's contract to be covered by revenue

33:43.687 --> 33:46.848
from property taxes? Was revenue from the other sources projected to fall

33:46.960 --> 33:51.055
below the needed amount to cover the contract amount, or are there

33:51.555 --> 33:55.149
other budget areas that need a roughly $4 million increase and this tax hike is

33:55.649 --> 33:58.698
being done under the guise of public safety because that is an easier sell than

33:58.762 --> 34:02.178
other programs? With this switch from using the general

34:02.210 --> 34:05.321
fund along with property taxes to only

34:05.353 --> 34:09.137
using property taxes for the sheriff, will the general fund be reduced

34:09.637 --> 34:13.257
a proportionate amount to reflect the change, or is the city— total city budget

34:13.289 --> 34:17.217
raising the $6 million? With the increase in sheriff

34:17.717 --> 34:21.130
deputies, is there any changes to the contract to make sure we are being protected

34:21.466 --> 34:25.683
and that the increased presence won't be used for generating revenue through tickets or over-policing

34:25.779 --> 34:30.058
as seen in neighborhood cities such as Saratoga Springs and American Fork? I understand,

34:30.122 --> 34:33.135
but have my disagreements with, the comments made by the Sheriff's Office and the City

34:33.167 --> 34:37.589
Council that Eagle Mountain could use a larger police force. I also understand there

34:37.637 --> 34:40.265
has not been a property tax hike in Eagle Mountain for a number of years.

34:40.842 --> 34:44.127
These 2 things being understood, why did the City Council feel the need to swap

34:44.627 --> 34:47.748
100% of the costs, including the $2 million increase, in one year?

34:48.293 --> 34:52.155
Could it not be possible to continue using alternative revenue sources for the Sheriff's Office

34:52.395 --> 34:55.664
with a modest increase to property taxes to cover the $2 million increase?

34:56.278 --> 34:59.823
Why was there the need to switch the entire $10 million over to property taxes?

35:00.421 --> 35:03.690
This seems— this just seems to me, and I imagine a number of folks here,

35:03.804 --> 35:06.700
a dramatic increase to the size and scope of the city under the guise of

35:06.716 --> 35:10.696
public safety to avoid having to have discussion or try and sell a less popular

35:11.196 --> 35:11.845
budget item. Thank you.

35:14.822 --> 35:15.485
Andrew Burke.

35:23.699 --> 35:27.076
My name's Andrew Burke. I've been here a couple times, a couple years back,

35:27.478 --> 35:30.839
like 5 years ago, and then recently moved here after we built our home last

35:31.339 --> 35:34.786
year. I'm gonna make this short. I do agree that the police

35:35.286 --> 35:38.505
office, the Sheriff's Department has to be supported. I do believe that, you know,

35:38.521 --> 35:41.400
we do need to, based off the research that I've done, we do need to

35:41.900 --> 35:45.078
increase it 0.45 over 1,000 residents versus

35:45.176 --> 35:48.822
the average of about 0.8. I mean, some of the stuff the chief deputy said

35:49.322 --> 35:52.067
wasn't accurate, like Saratoga's at 1.56 per thousand,

35:52.696 --> 35:55.852
but I'm not going to go into the semantics. Um, I do agree with the

35:56.352 --> 36:00.086
previous speaker that I don't think that the property taxes should be

36:00.456 --> 36:02.726
the thing that's covering all the increases.

36:04.028 --> 36:07.537
And I think my biggest issue, and I think most people would agree,

36:08.459 --> 36:12.195
is that the transparency is just not there. Why can't you give

36:12.695 --> 36:16.761
us— if you've allotted a certain amount for improvements

36:17.355 --> 36:20.810
under the guise of public safety, why can't

36:21.310 --> 36:23.845
you give us an itemized report before you say, yeah, we're voting on this?

36:23.976 --> 36:25.348
Let us know what you're increasing.

36:28.100 --> 36:31.995
So, I mean, it's frustrating because everybody is

36:32.495 --> 36:36.519
struggling. It's harder. Like, I heard a comment about AI. A lot

36:37.019 --> 36:39.746
of us don't know if we're going to have jobs in 2 years. Because AI

36:40.246 --> 36:43.984
is taking away the workforce. And,

36:44.001 --> 36:47.438
you know, now to sit there and say, hey, 220% right now,

36:47.908 --> 36:51.876
we haven't done it in 15 years, right now, without gradually

36:51.892 --> 36:54.917
rolling it out, it's almost criminal.

36:56.317 --> 36:59.500
Like, why would you— why would you do that to us? You were—

36:59.710 --> 37:02.699
we voted for you, and this is how you repay us?

37:03.507 --> 37:06.628
Now, I'm not against Increasing the budget for our sheriffs.

37:07.304 --> 37:11.599
Public— that is public safety. But $6.7,

37:11.711 --> 37:15.146
almost $8 million increased with no itemized budget?

37:15.628 --> 37:16.640
That's not acceptable.

37:19.367 --> 37:22.302
So my question is, if you are going to do this, can we get an

37:22.431 --> 37:25.979
itemized line for line on how every dollar is going to be spent?

37:28.279 --> 37:30.923
Because if you're not going to do that, then don't pass the bill.

37:34.057 --> 37:34.615
That's my time.

37:39.710 --> 37:40.194
Kelly Horton?

37:46.121 --> 37:48.091
I don't see Kelly. Can I take his time?

37:49.605 --> 37:52.759
I'm not on the list. You can— Can I take her time?

37:53.633 --> 37:57.257
You can fill out a paper. I'm right here. Oh, you're there. Oh, I'm sorry.

37:57.775 --> 38:00.916
No worries. It's all right,

38:01.500 --> 38:05.073
you can take your own time. My name is Kelly

38:05.089 --> 38:08.454
Horton. I've been here since 2016. You know, I first want

38:08.954 --> 38:12.077
to begin by saying that, you know, we really do support our public safety

38:12.093 --> 38:15.344
here. We love our law enforcement out here. I don't think anybody's going to disagree

38:15.426 --> 38:18.681
with that. Our firefighters, first responders, everything they do

38:19.181 --> 38:22.422
every day. It's not about whether they deserve support. They absolutely do.

38:22.894 --> 38:27.012
I said this is about whether asking residents to shoulder such a substantial

38:27.108 --> 38:29.979
tax increases the only or the best solution.

38:30.653 --> 38:34.117
Many of us are already struggling. The cost of groceries,

38:34.166 --> 38:37.085
utilities, insurance, and housing has increased dramatically.

38:37.630 --> 38:41.271
Families are making difficult choices every month just to stay afloat.

38:41.785 --> 38:45.698
For people living on fixed incomes, seniors, and residents with disabilities,

38:46.115 --> 38:49.484
even a few hundred dollars a year can make the difference between paying bills and

38:49.984 --> 38:54.071
falling behind. You know, before asking taxpayers to pay more, I respectfully ask,

38:54.296 --> 38:57.893
You know, what specific spending reductions were made before deciding

38:57.925 --> 39:01.907
to raise taxes? You know, what programs or projects were delayed or

39:01.939 --> 39:05.391
eliminated to demonstrate that every other option has been exhausted?

39:06.098 --> 39:09.630
You know, why is the increase— this increase being proposed all at once

39:10.130 --> 39:14.110
instead of being phased in over several years? You know, what guarantees

39:14.142 --> 39:17.948
can you provide that this won't become the new normal with additional

39:17.996 --> 39:21.818
large increases in the future? How will the city measure whether

39:21.915 --> 39:24.871
these additional tax dollars actually improve public safety,

39:25.289 --> 39:27.441
and will those results be reported publicly?

39:28.020 --> 39:31.859
Transparency matters. Residents deserve to know exactly

39:31.956 --> 39:35.073
where every additional dollar will go, how success will

39:35.105 --> 39:38.350
be measured, and what accountability exists if the

39:38.382 --> 39:42.543
expected results are not achieved. You know, Eagle Mountain has grown rapidly.

39:42.736 --> 39:46.479
That growth has brought challenges, but it's also brought additional homes,

39:46.910 --> 39:50.432
businesses, and a broader tax base. I ask that the council

39:50.496 --> 39:53.955
to, to please explain what that growth alone— why that growth

39:54.003 --> 39:57.415
alone is not enough to help meet these needs. And most importantly,

39:57.463 --> 40:01.426
please remember that behind every tax bill is a family. You know,

40:01.458 --> 40:04.903
for, for some, this may seem like a budget decision, but for

40:05.403 --> 40:08.775
residents, it's groceries, it's medicine, it's gas, it's schools,

40:08.807 --> 40:12.659
clothes, it's child care, or keeping a roof over our heads.

40:13.261 --> 40:16.629
You know, I respectfully ask the council to reconsider the size and timing

40:16.678 --> 40:20.209
of this increase. If additional funding is truly necessary,

40:20.241 --> 40:23.526
consider a phased approach. Continue identifying spending

40:23.558 --> 40:27.431
efficiencies and ensure residents are fully informed before placing a greater

40:27.704 --> 40:30.082
financial burden on them. Thank you for your time.

40:33.674 --> 40:34.294
Anthony Wood.

40:45.777 --> 40:47.453
My name is Anthony. Um,

40:48.694 --> 40:53.110
so true, true representation means reflecting the will of your constituents.

40:53.884 --> 40:57.862
When you must convince us of your narrative, then that's manipulation.

40:59.484 --> 41:02.814
The tax increase is being advertised as a need for increase in

41:03.314 --> 41:07.105
law enforcement. The supporting stats that are being used are how many

41:07.605 --> 41:09.747
officers there are per 1,000 citizens.

41:11.570 --> 41:14.693
I don't like that. I don't like that number. What I do think we should

41:15.193 --> 41:18.412
be looking at is the crime rates. So if we're using some of the comparative

41:18.912 --> 41:22.097
cities you guys were using in the— in the how many officers per capita,

41:22.659 --> 41:26.146
Sandy is 32 in 1,000. Means you're going to be— you have

41:26.259 --> 41:29.505
a chance of being a victim 32 times out

41:30.005 --> 41:33.509
of 1,000. For Lehigh, it's 22 per 1,000. Do you

41:34.009 --> 41:38.021
guys have any idea what Eagle Mountain is? It is 1 to 1.2

41:38.234 --> 41:41.450
per 1,000. Our crime rate is very low.

41:42.460 --> 41:45.730
We see our officers, multiple vehicles per stop.

41:45.778 --> 41:49.467
That's what we get to see as citizens. 4— 3 squad cars,

41:49.564 --> 41:53.536
4 squad cars per stop, per incident. We see

41:54.036 --> 41:56.659
them at the gas stations. It doesn't look like they're crazy busy. Right.

41:57.268 --> 42:00.453
They may need some support, but this is the wrong way to go about it.

42:01.128 --> 42:04.007
You're asking the wrong people to pay for this.

42:04.441 --> 42:06.743
What I mean is that there are a lot of corporations, like we were talking

42:06.791 --> 42:09.848
about with the data centers, that are getting those tax breaks.

42:11.304 --> 42:15.120
They do a lot of damage to our infrastructure, our water, our roads,

42:15.492 --> 42:19.366
and they're not contributing to that. I was looking at the repairs to Pony Express,

42:19.912 --> 42:23.752
and it took us the end of '24 and '25

42:23.864 --> 42:26.582
to finish Pony Express, and I went on there the very next day and I

42:27.082 --> 42:30.116
rode it. I ride a motorcycle and I rode it. It's garbage.

42:31.145 --> 42:34.297
I don't know how much you guys spent on that, but it's trash. It needs

42:34.797 --> 42:36.822
to be done again. Who signed off in saying that that was okay?

42:40.544 --> 42:43.827
Another example about the spending, and like, I would like to

42:43.843 --> 42:46.997
focus on budgeting what we have first before

42:47.497 --> 42:50.813
we ask for more. And another example that I have concerns with,

42:51.298 --> 42:54.533
with how we spend our money is that in 2022, in August, we spent—

42:55.033 --> 42:59.109
we sent $1.13 million

42:59.609 --> 43:03.613
to a scammer. Just money gone. Like, we need to budget what we

43:04.113 --> 43:08.010
have before we ask for more. I agree, we may need more,

43:08.686 --> 43:11.656
but I need to focus on the budget before we get there. I mean,

43:12.157 --> 43:15.779
I don't lend money to family members and friends that are irresponsible

43:15.795 --> 43:18.026
with money, and I don't want to do the same thing here. Can you say

43:18.526 --> 43:19.789
that again? I don't want to give you more money. I don't trust you guys

43:19.837 --> 43:23.038
with it. I mean, sending money to a scammer, I have to teach my grandma

43:23.168 --> 43:25.371
not to do that. I don't want to have to teach you guys not to

43:29.610 --> 43:30.247
That's all I have.

43:33.330 --> 43:34.101
Bruno Hunsaker.

43:46.781 --> 43:49.878
I don't know about following all these guys that's been up here.

43:49.959 --> 43:50.888
Some great comments.

43:53.732 --> 43:56.971
I'm just going to represent the old guys or the old

43:57.471 --> 44:00.712
women. We're the seniors. So most people on Social

44:01.212 --> 44:05.539
Security, the average, like Brett's mom, is probably $1,300 or $1,400

44:05.876 --> 44:09.492
a month because she's been on it. I'm about $1,800,

44:09.556 --> 44:12.936
so I'm a little more fortunate. So I give you $300 extra.

44:14.066 --> 44:17.696
And so— and we're on a fixed income. I'm lucky

44:17.760 --> 44:20.982
I still work part-time, so it's not going to affect me as much. But these

44:21.016 --> 44:23.796
young families that they've all been talking about.

44:24.166 --> 44:27.506
So we get $300 there. And those of you that don't know what's going to

44:28.006 --> 44:31.473
happen next year when this mighty new school district comes

44:31.973 --> 44:35.600
in that you were all buffaloed into voting for,

44:36.611 --> 44:40.208
they're going to start out $200 million in the hole. So if

44:40.708 --> 44:44.577
you think the City Council is going to charge you $300

44:44.625 --> 44:48.720
more on a $500,000 home, you wait till next year's

44:48.736 --> 44:53.234
tax intrication when the district is going to raise that

44:53.734 --> 44:56.962
up probably $300 to $400 plus a bond the next year.

44:57.573 --> 45:00.597
They need 17 schools in the next 15 years,

45:01.032 --> 45:05.045
and they're a pretty small school district to do that. So I'm just telling you,

45:05.384 --> 45:09.666
I hope you all show up next year in total force when

45:10.166 --> 45:12.729
that school board meets to increase your taxes.

45:14.416 --> 45:17.670
And also, I agree on some of those roads because I ride

45:18.170 --> 45:21.717
a bike too, and It's supposed to be a soft tail, but it really is

45:22.217 --> 45:24.996
a hard tail on that road. So anyway,

45:26.902 --> 45:30.150
I support law enforcement. I don't know what the crime rate

45:30.650 --> 45:34.258
is. I'm thinking per capita,

45:34.663 --> 45:37.947
it might be as bad as West Valley City because all I ever hear is

45:38.303 --> 45:42.209
domestic this and domestic that. They're doing their job,

45:42.225 --> 45:45.635
and I know they need an increase. Thank you. But like everybody else said,

45:46.261 --> 45:50.046
how many building permits? We had the most building permits in the state

45:50.546 --> 45:54.344
of Utah in Eagle Mountain last year. And then I see them build

45:54.376 --> 45:58.418
2 homes over by Blackridge, and they brought gravel

45:58.482 --> 46:01.899
in, compacted a little bit, and put these 2 new homes in just

46:02.399 --> 46:05.876
to get a building permit. I'm starting to wonder if people will sell somebody in

46:05.925 --> 46:07.641
their family for a building permit.

46:08.555 --> 46:12.100
Just that much— those building permits and those impact fees should

46:12.600 --> 46:15.947
be paying for what you're asking for. I know your minds

46:16.447 --> 46:19.586
are made up. I don't think you're going to budge. I think it's going to

46:19.634 --> 46:22.648
go through, and I know you feel our pain.

46:23.096 --> 46:27.537
So anyway, 30 seconds remaining. I appreciate the job you guys are doing,

46:28.274 --> 46:31.897
and I know it's a hard job, but I'm just telling people you're going to

46:32.397 --> 46:35.840
be paying a lot of money the next 3 years between this and the new

46:36.340 --> 46:39.719
school district. And the mayor tells me while he was a city councilman

46:40.218 --> 46:44.329
the water treatment plant needs to be updated next 4 years, there's another $50

46:44.782 --> 46:46.254
a month on top of that. Thank you.

46:49.214 --> 46:50.116
Nathan Thornburg.

46:59.491 --> 47:01.277
Hello, I'm Nathan Thornburg.

47:04.102 --> 47:07.243
Um, I can understand the way the state tax

47:07.938 --> 47:11.750
regulations and codes don't

47:12.380 --> 47:16.248
help increase revenue as property values

47:16.345 --> 47:16.882
increase.

47:19.440 --> 47:22.706
However, like everybody else, I have questions.

47:24.123 --> 47:27.953
Why wasn't— why was the campaign

47:28.738 --> 47:30.542
initially, that was initially released,

47:31.854 --> 47:35.286
that This is gonna 100%

47:35.689 --> 47:38.971
be to increase our public safety.

47:40.097 --> 47:43.136
The end. Period. And we were all,

47:43.412 --> 47:47.196
I think the way that the messaging was presented was we were all supposed

47:47.696 --> 47:51.329
to go, yes, yes.

47:52.333 --> 47:56.283
And it was only after members of our community actually

47:56.315 --> 47:59.643
pressed that there was more of an explanation

47:59.659 --> 48:03.150
given. This is going to free up money so that we can better

48:03.166 --> 48:06.853
improve things. I think we all would have loved to hear

48:06.986 --> 48:10.412
that initially, if money

48:10.525 --> 48:14.831
was— if there was a plan to increase revenue

48:15.264 --> 48:18.799
to improve the

48:18.864 --> 48:22.352
quality of life here in Eagle Mountain, you wouldn't be

48:22.852 --> 48:26.530
getting slammed right now. You probably still

48:26.644 --> 48:30.780
would be because 220%, as was stated earlier

48:32.089 --> 48:32.990
is almost criminal.

48:37.408 --> 48:40.729
Do you see how the changing of the narrative only after

48:41.229 --> 48:44.083
being pressed erodes trust? Now we don't know what to believe.

48:45.389 --> 48:48.961
You were either dishonest then or you're dishonest now.

48:50.562 --> 48:54.185
Anything you say to smooth it over can at best only

48:54.202 --> 48:57.728
be taken with a grain of salt. But most likely

48:58.228 --> 49:01.587
is just not going to be believed at all unless

49:04.107 --> 49:06.680
you start putting the actual money where your mouth is.

49:07.935 --> 49:11.504
I think it's safe to say that after tonight you have an assignment.

49:12.647 --> 49:16.334
What's the plan? Is there a proposed budget or schedule of

49:16.382 --> 49:20.005
these capital projects, uh, that the city intends to

49:20.505 --> 49:24.104
complete? And the only way to regain trust in this communities to follow through

49:24.313 --> 49:28.059
with what we need. And if there

49:28.123 --> 49:31.824
is no publicly released budget for us— 30

49:32.324 --> 49:35.676
seconds remaining. —to have access to so that we can, you know,

49:36.162 --> 49:39.398
maybe see— begin to see some

49:39.414 --> 49:43.076
of your intentions, if that isn't released to us,

49:45.230 --> 49:49.099
what are we left to believe? Are we supposed to just

49:49.599 --> 49:53.688
trust you? We don't trust you. If there is no

49:55.141 --> 49:56.254
line item given to us,

49:58.600 --> 49:59.428
what are we left with?

50:03.208 --> 50:09.601
Your time is up. Thank you. Matt Everett.

50:14.976 --> 50:17.937
Good evening, Council. Good evening, Mayor, wherever you are.

50:18.374 --> 50:20.743
I Um, stand to, uh,

50:21.513 --> 50:25.188
stand firmly in the minority opinion of the people that are in this room tonight.

50:25.846 --> 50:30.019
Um, I encourage you to pass this tax increase.

50:30.918 --> 50:34.288
Now, having said that, 220% is a big

50:34.788 --> 50:38.701
number. I wish it wasn't that big. I, knowing you and

50:39.201 --> 50:42.970
the interactions that I've had, I would assume that you probably have a similar

50:43.470 --> 50:47.190
feeling to that. In my opinion, 220% is a direct

50:47.690 --> 50:51.440
reflection of poor management and leadership that

50:51.940 --> 50:55.385
the city has had in the past 15-plus years. My family

50:55.885 --> 50:58.368
and I have lived in the city for about 17, a little over 17 years.

50:58.448 --> 51:01.239
I've raised my family here. I'm continuing to raise my family here.

51:02.040 --> 51:05.408
There are a lot of things that need to be improved in the city.

51:06.290 --> 51:09.530
Talk about roads. We've talked about infrastructure. We've talked about a lot of different things.

51:09.642 --> 51:13.753
All of those things cost money. And there's limited ways that

51:14.253 --> 51:17.753
the city's able to— Your actions— To take care of those needs and

51:18.253 --> 51:21.866
the requirements that they have. Moving the property

51:22.366 --> 51:25.931
taxes and using this increase to fund public safety

51:26.767 --> 51:30.205
makes it a stable fund that we're able— the city will be able to

51:30.705 --> 51:34.640
use those known dollars every year to fund the

51:35.140 --> 51:37.307
needs of the public safety.

51:38.060 --> 51:41.394
So this is a difficult night. This is gonna

51:41.894 --> 51:45.626
be a difficult thing for a lot of residents. I understand that. But I encourage

51:45.723 --> 51:48.879
you to continue on the path of leadership that

51:49.379 --> 51:53.033
you have and to make the hard decisions regardless

51:53.163 --> 51:55.674
of what the outcomes of those will be. Thank you.

51:59.481 --> 52:00.226
Mark McConkey.

52:12.278 --> 52:15.473
Others have talked about their frustration that these funds aren't being— aren't

52:15.489 --> 52:18.845
actually being used for public safety, and I feel that pain, especially as the funds

52:18.942 --> 52:22.057
we use for public safety now get sent out of the— out to the county

52:22.795 --> 52:26.665
rather than being used to establish our own public safety through a city police department

52:27.165 --> 52:30.438
accountable to the mayor and this council. Eagle Mountain is the largest city in Utah

52:30.503 --> 52:33.907
without its own dedicated city police department. And looking

52:34.407 --> 52:38.388
at the state's border in Utah, we're the second largest city without a police department.

52:38.612 --> 52:41.920
Only Centennial in Colorado is bigger. In fact, if we were

52:42.420 --> 52:44.056
to take a deeper dive on this and take a look at the size of

52:44.072 --> 52:47.284
the largest cities in each of the states without a police department, here's what we'd

52:47.784 --> 52:51.283
see. Eagle Mountain is twice the size of Kuna, Idaho, their largest city.

52:52.278 --> 52:55.490
We're 3 times larger than Fernley, Nevada, their largest city without a

52:55.990 --> 52:59.096
police department. We're 4.6 times larger than Castle Pines, Colorado,

52:59.161 --> 53:02.958
which is their second after Centennial. We're 3.1 times

53:03.006 --> 53:06.676
larger than Fountain Hills, Arizona, and we're a whopping 37.8 times

53:06.772 --> 53:09.833
larger than Pinedale, Wyoming, which is their largest city without a city

53:10.333 --> 53:14.079
police department. We've outgrown the point where we should rely on, on county support rather

53:14.579 --> 53:18.230
than owning that ourselves. Every dollar that we send to the county for policing is

53:18.730 --> 53:21.323
a dollar that we give to be controlled by the county, and every decision about

53:21.355 --> 53:24.659
how our streets are patrolled is made by people who don't answer to this council

53:25.159 --> 53:28.429
or to the residents of Eagle Mountain. Right now, as we contract with the county

53:28.929 --> 53:32.969
sheriff, that means we have no direct say over hiring standards, use of force policy,

53:33.242 --> 53:35.600
response priorities, or community policing style.

53:36.435 --> 53:39.130
Those decisions are made for the whole county and are not tailored to us.

53:39.579 --> 53:43.381
If we ever disagree with those decisions, we don't have the ability to push for

53:43.881 --> 53:47.440
those changes outside of election season. Even during election season, Eagle Mountain

53:47.940 --> 53:50.825
only accounts for 10% of the voter population in Utah County, and there may well

53:50.889 --> 53:54.097
be some elections where where the sheriff runs unopposed, as he is this

53:54.597 --> 53:58.089
year, which limits our options even more. A city police chief would

53:58.589 --> 54:01.504
answer to the mayor and to this council and its residents, getting a clear line

54:01.616 --> 54:05.480
of accountability. I know the first objection is going to be cost, especially startup

54:05.980 --> 54:08.927
costs, but the city already owns the building the sheriff's department operates out of right

54:09.427 --> 54:12.759
here in Eagle Mountain. If we convert that city to a police department, there's no

54:12.791 --> 54:16.431
new facility building or lease. That overhead already exists.

54:16.864 --> 54:20.391
Because our contract with the county sheriff's department accounts for about 1/3 of their budget,

54:20.520 --> 54:23.779
likely be able to transition many of their officers to city officer positions

54:24.279 --> 54:28.098
as well, reducing costs of hiring and training. We're not building departments from

54:28.598 --> 54:32.337
scratch, we're being able to convert what's already here. Beyond that, the startup

54:32.353 --> 54:35.773
and transition costs will only be higher in the future as our population grows.

54:36.448 --> 54:39.707
When it comes to our policing options, I see 3 options:

54:40.301 --> 54:44.299
start a police department now, start a police department sometime in the future— 30 seconds

54:44.799 --> 54:48.160
remaining. —as our population grows, or never start a police department and

54:48.176 --> 54:51.300
be okay with not having control over our police force. So my ask

54:51.800 --> 54:55.102
tonight is to conduct a study of the cost for standing up a municipal police

54:55.602 --> 54:59.439
department. As we earmark these funds for public safety, let's use these funds in

54:59.939 --> 55:01.190
a way that we can control. Thank you.

55:03.697 --> 55:04.805
Betty Peralta.

55:14.336 --> 55:16.820
Good evening. My name is Betty Peralta,

55:17.845 --> 55:21.739
and I'm here to oppose the increase, and these

55:21.803 --> 55:25.650
are comments I have. The proposed

55:26.150 --> 55:29.880
increase, I feel, is outrageous. The justification is not

55:30.380 --> 55:33.886
clear enough. The homeowner property rates increase,

55:34.752 --> 55:38.219
and as our income remains the same. The property

55:38.299 --> 55:41.665
values, especially in my community, which is Sweetwater,

55:41.746 --> 55:45.836
continue to fall. Eagle Mountain city center and communities

55:45.949 --> 55:47.439
look more run-down every day.

55:49.111 --> 55:52.877
My property value alone has decreased $7,000 in 2 months.

55:53.347 --> 55:57.048
So yes, I agree with the previous speakers that

55:57.548 --> 56:01.157
this is criminal to impose a tax rate

56:01.576 --> 56:06.100
increase of this kind. The traffic has increased here significantly.

56:06.539 --> 56:10.765
The roads are horrible. And the

56:12.945 --> 56:16.625
majority of homeowners, I'm asking to oppose this increase.

56:17.529 --> 56:21.903
And my other question is, because it has not been outright

56:22.403 --> 56:25.743
and truthful what these funds are being used for, are we using any

56:25.775 --> 56:28.452
of these funds for city council staff pay increases?

56:29.806 --> 56:33.626
I'm all in for safety and first responders. I'm a retired

56:33.933 --> 56:38.383
38-year first responder, so I know that those are essential

56:38.883 --> 56:42.656
and necessary needs for Eagle Mountain, but I cannot justify the

56:43.156 --> 56:43.801
increase. Thank you.

56:48.211 --> 56:51.071
Joseph Pill— I don't know how to say it.

56:51.136 --> 56:54.327
Not even close. Thank you. It's French. Not even close.

56:55.905 --> 56:58.396
First of all, I just wanna say— I'm sorry, hold on, Joseph, will you say

56:58.412 --> 57:01.228
it for the record? Oh, Joseph Pedlow.

57:02.700 --> 57:04.844
All right, so first I wanna say I don't wanna be being in your seats

57:05.061 --> 57:08.490
tonight. It's probably not a fun meeting. But I

57:08.990 --> 57:11.741
do wanna thank you for your service and the commitments, 'cause you wouldn't have run

57:12.241 --> 57:14.836
for this position if you didn't want it. The big thing I wanna say is

57:14.932 --> 57:18.986
just urging caution. So I work in higher education

57:19.486 --> 57:22.342
in the state, and I've worked there for about 10 years. And over those times,

57:22.407 --> 57:26.099
we've seen again and again when the state legislature has proposed big budget increases

57:26.599 --> 57:29.839
and big budget pushes, and there'll be community blowup and hard feelings,

57:29.871 --> 57:32.937
and often it gets redacted. And I think we can learn a lesson from that.

57:33.403 --> 57:36.582
I don't think anyone here doesn't want to help our officers. We do.

57:36.999 --> 57:39.343
We want them to be the best officers in the county. We want them to

57:39.843 --> 57:42.955
have the resources they need. But I think we also can all

57:43.455 --> 57:46.663
agree that 220% is a lot at once, especially since a lot of us are

57:47.163 --> 57:50.660
nervous about the new school district. about water facilities, road infrastructure,

57:51.160 --> 57:54.020
more infrastructure as the city grows. We're one of the fastest growing cities in Utah.

57:54.780 --> 57:58.540
So my hope would be just to urge caution because we don't

57:59.040 --> 58:01.120
know what it's going to be like in 3 years. We don't know if the

58:01.620 --> 58:04.220
new school district is going to ask for a 300% increase because they don't have

58:04.720 --> 58:07.980
administrative buildings, they don't have a bus depot, they don't have the mechanics. We don't

58:08.480 --> 58:10.580
know that. We don't know what the water will be. We don't know what the

58:11.080 --> 58:14.030
infrastructure will be. And we do know we are getting more stores. We're getting Lowe's.

58:14.200 --> 58:18.084
We're getting Smith's, and we will see that income increase as the hospital

58:18.584 --> 58:21.790
comes out here and as other plans happen. But we just don't know what that

58:22.290 --> 58:25.881
is right now. But we do know 220% is a lot to

58:26.381 --> 58:29.490
ask, especially since transparency has been an issue for a lot of residents.

58:30.068 --> 58:33.918
So my only advice is just caution, because maybe this is

58:33.966 --> 58:37.271
where we do need to be, and maybe you have very important reasons. I believe

58:37.771 --> 58:40.784
you're all amazing people who aren't increasing this for no reason. Thank you.

58:41.522 --> 58:44.477
But we can all agree that this is a bit of a shock in the

58:44.977 --> 58:49.037
community, and you probably don't have this typical turnout at events like this because

58:49.069 --> 58:52.361
we're shocked at the number, and we're shocked at the fact that we don't know

58:52.505 --> 58:55.893
exactly what the general fund that's gonna be increasing by about $5 million,

58:56.359 --> 59:00.116
what's that meant for? So my only advice is just to urge

59:00.148 --> 59:03.376
caution, maybe do a smaller increase. Let us see what the new revenues will

59:03.876 --> 59:06.250
be when we get more infrastructure. Let's see what the new property value revenues will

59:06.750 --> 59:09.183
be. Let us see what the store of news will be, and then let us

59:09.296 --> 59:12.071
know what we need to do. Because I think no one here is opposed to

59:12.297 --> 59:15.926
bettering our city and bettering our police force. I think what we are opposed

59:16.426 --> 59:18.712
to is making a jump in the dark. So thank you.

59:21.032 --> 59:21.643
Josh Shadd.

59:29.467 --> 59:31.911
My name is Josh Shadd. I've been a resident here for about 12 years.

59:33.794 --> 59:36.198
Really came to me as a shock that you guys are going to increase the

59:36.698 --> 59:39.966
taxes by 220%. So I just have some comments I wrote

59:40.466 --> 59:43.156
down. With the increased tax revenue that will be added to the general fund and

59:43.656 --> 59:47.372
used for capital projects, it's a little deceitful to present, present this

59:47.420 --> 59:50.787
as 100% funding towards public safety, as the previously allocated

59:51.287 --> 59:54.650
funds are now set into the general fund and used for capital projects.

59:55.419 --> 59:58.401
As we build out housing in Eagle Mountain, property taxes should increase,

59:58.417 --> 01:00:01.482
and Why haven't those funds been properly allocated in the budget?

01:00:02.573 --> 01:00:05.590
And just to clarify, I don't have any issue with increasing policing,

01:00:06.504 --> 01:00:09.938
police presence within the city limits of Eagle Mountain. The issue I have is the

01:00:10.438 --> 01:00:14.543
communication of this city council to its members, to the residents

01:00:15.043 --> 01:00:18.699
of Eagle Mountain, and being clear with your guys' intention of what you

01:00:19.199 --> 01:00:23.352
intend to do with our tax dollars. This is something that I have brought

01:00:23.852 --> 01:00:27.798
up before, is communication from this city hall. The city hall is terrible

01:00:28.071 --> 01:00:31.590
at messaging. You guys are terrible at communicating meetings.

01:00:32.008 --> 01:00:35.654
You guys are terrible at reaching out to the citizens.

01:00:36.345 --> 01:00:38.842
The only reason I saw this is because I happen to go on Facebook.

01:00:38.923 --> 01:00:42.081
I've signed up for all your newsletters, all your text messages. I go on the

01:00:42.581 --> 01:00:45.681
website every once in a while, but I have a life outside of this city,

01:00:46.449 --> 01:00:48.458
so you guys need to be better at messaging.

01:00:50.310 --> 01:00:53.626
Previous city councils have also failed to to take— to be

01:00:53.690 --> 01:00:57.288
good stewards of our taxpayer dollars. Convince us that this

01:00:57.401 --> 01:01:01.223
tax increase for the taxpayers is going

01:01:01.239 --> 01:01:05.881
to not be wasted and misallocated

01:01:05.913 --> 01:01:09.576
and spent on things that are not in the budget or are hidden

01:01:10.170 --> 01:01:14.089
or moved to the side. On another note, I do believe

01:01:14.105 --> 01:01:17.414
we have had a utility rate increase that's supposed

01:01:17.914 --> 01:01:21.506
to happen over the next couple years, and that is in addition

01:01:22.006 --> 01:01:25.456
to this. So you guys are going to be putting undue stress on the normal

01:01:25.956 --> 01:01:30.177
families of Eagle Mountain. And I think that's pretty

01:01:30.677 --> 01:01:31.948
much it I got. Thank you guys for your time.

01:01:33.803 --> 01:01:34.770
Mark Espinoza.

01:01:34.995 --> 01:01:39.005
Council,

01:01:44.768 --> 01:01:48.220
Thank you for having this meeting. Sure, big turnout here. I hear a lot of

01:01:48.253 --> 01:01:51.418
people concerned. My big concern is,

01:01:52.016 --> 01:01:55.280
guys, I, I had a business,

01:01:56.303 --> 01:01:59.886
made a payroll and stuff. All the things that you

01:02:00.259 --> 01:02:03.935
need to do to run a business, you got to make. But guys,

01:02:04.941 --> 01:02:08.771
220% increase? If I did that to my customers, I'd be out

01:02:09.271 --> 01:02:13.017
of business. So we got to do something. Everybody's so fed

01:02:13.517 --> 01:02:18.443
up that 220%— if it's

01:02:18.491 --> 01:02:22.890
3%, you would have had half a crowd in here. But you go to— you

01:02:23.390 --> 01:02:26.662
hit it big, 220%. Maybe go back.

01:02:26.983 --> 01:02:29.054
I don't know if we have time or if you're going to vote on this.

01:02:29.472 --> 01:02:32.506
If you're going to vote on this tonight, we're pretty much, pretty much done.

01:02:33.501 --> 01:02:36.391
You got to go back and look. How can we bring up revenue?

01:02:37.116 --> 01:02:41.173
I hope the mayor is doing something. I wish he was here instead

01:02:41.673 --> 01:02:45.263
of thinking that he's looking at a video on Zoom. I wish he was in

01:02:45.763 --> 01:02:49.314
front of us looking at all these people here. But if he's making a

01:02:49.814 --> 01:02:52.218
great deal for Eagle Mountain, fantastic.

01:02:52.766 --> 01:02:55.709
He's got my approval. But I don't think so.

01:02:57.176 --> 01:03:01.060
It's important. You got a lot of people here, a lot

01:03:01.560 --> 01:03:04.485
of things, especially out here on the communication with you guys. Thank you.

01:03:06.104 --> 01:03:09.921
Go on your website, put a link on there, and then it— line

01:03:10.002 --> 01:03:13.576
item be— line item. It'll show everybody what's going

01:03:13.656 --> 01:03:17.368
on. But again, bringing out

01:03:17.868 --> 01:03:21.209
the 220— come on, guys. You know

01:03:21.225 --> 01:03:23.593
better. I heard some people here in businesses.

01:03:24.920 --> 01:03:28.511
Shoot, you do that to your customers and see how long you're in business.

01:03:29.583 --> 01:03:33.336
Again, I heard fixed

01:03:33.836 --> 01:03:36.169
incomes and stuff. I came from California,

01:03:37.173 --> 01:03:41.474
a lot worse. They don't even listen. It got so bad, I had

01:03:41.490 --> 01:03:45.092
to move. I'm glad I moved to Eagle Mountain.

01:03:45.221 --> 01:03:48.052
I love the place. Family-oriented, love it.

01:03:49.022 --> 01:03:52.274
But do not, do not go down that road. There's a

01:03:52.338 --> 01:03:56.185
reason why people move out of California. It's not the poor

01:03:56.685 --> 01:03:58.517
people. It's the rich people. People with money,

01:03:58.614 --> 01:04:01.456
and they come in to spend the money.

01:04:02.355 --> 01:04:05.630
Keep them in Eagle Mountain. That's one way to get the revenue. Other ways,

01:04:06.369 --> 01:04:09.741
get some bigger people in businesses. That's how you generate

01:04:10.241 --> 01:04:14.076
money into the coffers. Again, I thank

01:04:14.576 --> 01:04:17.593
you guys. 30 seconds remaining. I thank you guys for listening to us,

01:04:18.106 --> 01:04:21.398
but I hope, I really hope you hear everybody, what they had to say.

01:04:22.909 --> 01:04:27.166
I'm retired. I can come up here. I was ticked off working

01:04:27.263 --> 01:04:31.121
30 years, buying a business, ticked off. I couldn't go to these meetings.

01:04:31.234 --> 01:04:33.374
Shoot, 13, 14 hours a day.

01:04:34.946 --> 01:04:38.805
Well, now I'm retired. I could do some more. Thank you

01:04:39.111 --> 01:04:42.830
again, and thanks for everybody coming out. Be sure

01:04:43.330 --> 01:04:47.032
to vote. Be sure to vote. Thank you. Your time is

01:04:47.096 --> 01:04:49.031
up. Thank you. Jeff Ruth.

01:05:07.475 --> 01:05:11.197
Hey, counsel. Jared. I'm going to be

01:05:11.697 --> 01:05:17.579
the ad bono, aside from Matt, I think. But I'm

01:05:18.079 --> 01:05:21.001
a little frustrated because this is going to impact me.

01:05:21.953 --> 01:05:27.192
But I can't tell you how many times I've called for an officer and

01:05:27.208 --> 01:05:30.248
they don't show up. Yeah, it was kind of minor on the list of things

01:05:30.831 --> 01:05:34.443
that were probably going on, but they didn't show up. Once in

01:05:34.459 --> 01:05:37.361
a while I get a call and say, hey, we're sorry, you know, we didn't

01:05:37.377 --> 01:05:41.137
make it. But We had this

01:05:41.637 --> 01:05:45.046
going on. Okay, that's fine. I've called for other things.

01:05:45.222 --> 01:05:48.342
Hey, we only got 2 officers on duty this morning.

01:05:48.938 --> 01:05:52.239
We can't come out right now. All right,

01:05:52.288 --> 01:05:55.902
fine. I've asked, why don't

01:05:55.919 --> 01:05:59.582
the officers out here do preventative? We can only do

01:05:59.711 --> 01:06:06.227
reactive. We don't have enough officers to do Preventative

01:06:06.487 --> 01:06:09.622
calls. I can't tell you all the vandalism I've seen

01:06:09.671 --> 01:06:12.335
over at Corey Ride. I mean, it's ridiculous.

01:06:13.300 --> 01:06:16.446
Every once in a while, an officer should be sitting out there and catch some

01:06:16.478 --> 01:06:19.705
of these teens out there busting things up, busting up

01:06:20.205 --> 01:06:24.046
the bathrooms and everything else. And I understand

01:06:24.709 --> 01:06:28.819
you're going to shift the money for the officers into

01:06:28.835 --> 01:06:32.182
their kind of their own separate account. And that's going to free up other

01:06:32.682 --> 01:06:35.563
money. How many times have I been up here and asked you guys to mow

01:06:35.709 --> 01:06:38.879
along the roads, to fix this, to fix that?

01:06:39.800 --> 01:06:43.055
Well, it's my understanding that if you move the money,

01:06:44.771 --> 01:06:47.142
then you'll have the money to do this other stuff.

01:06:49.179 --> 01:06:51.276
I mean, it's like with the voles at the park.

01:06:52.824 --> 01:06:56.179
Max, I think, got hurt because he— his leg went into one of those holes.

01:06:56.666 --> 01:06:59.621
I've asked it to be addressed. Never,

01:07:00.295 --> 01:07:03.876
never done. Um, so I mean,

01:07:04.052 --> 01:07:07.761
I love our officers. I met many of them. I've dealt with them, and they're

01:07:08.261 --> 01:07:11.567
good. I think we need this. Like I said, it's going to impact me

01:07:11.615 --> 01:07:15.517
a lot. I'm on Social Security. It's going to be tough.

01:07:16.095 --> 01:07:18.969
Me and Melissa talked, I think it was at the convention, about this,

01:07:19.948 --> 01:07:24.188
and I understand. Thank you. It's just—

01:07:24.301 --> 01:07:27.257
but it gets me. People say, well, bring in more businesses.

01:07:27.819 --> 01:07:30.759
Every time a big business wants to come in here,

01:07:31.450 --> 01:07:34.117
what do you get? You can't bring that in here.

01:07:34.807 --> 01:07:37.956
Oh, it's going to use too much water, too much electricity, this and that.

01:07:38.422 --> 01:07:41.667
It just drives me crazy. 30 seconds remaining. Um,

01:07:42.470 --> 01:07:46.567
so like I said, how many people here

01:07:46.615 --> 01:07:49.041
would vote for a rec center even if it was 300%?

01:07:50.957 --> 01:07:54.538
So I hope you pass this. Get us some officers out there to

01:07:55.038 --> 01:07:59.660
help us out. Thank you.

01:08:00.619 --> 01:08:01.492
Denver Dorrell.

01:08:14.427 --> 01:08:16.002
Hi. I didn't come up here prepared.

01:08:18.849 --> 01:08:22.036
Life, liberty, and pursuit of happiness. The American dream.

01:08:23.459 --> 01:08:26.877
That's what I've always wanted. Eagle Mountain was

01:08:27.154 --> 01:08:30.009
the first place I was able to actually achieve that.

01:08:32.342 --> 01:08:35.341
And I'm gonna tell you right now, I'm stressed out, panicked,

01:08:36.152 --> 01:08:38.729
because that American dream is about to turn into a nightmare.

01:08:40.786 --> 01:08:44.145
I am in a single Income household.

01:08:45.746 --> 01:08:49.174
Yeah, I make good money, but, you know, I got

01:08:50.144 --> 01:08:53.844
everything else going on. Um, I don't think anybody here would argue

01:08:54.748 --> 01:08:58.008
setting money aside for the Sheriff's Department, first responders,

01:08:58.912 --> 01:09:02.774
because, you know, my family alone has benefited so much

01:09:02.790 --> 01:09:06.824
from them. You know, with my 4-year-old daughter who has more flight hours

01:09:06.921 --> 01:09:09.300
in a Life Flight than the pilot himself.

01:09:11.899 --> 01:09:15.391
My son, who was shot in his neck, you know, right before

01:09:15.440 --> 01:09:19.027
Christmas, one of the sheriff's deputies stuck her

01:09:19.527 --> 01:09:22.666
finger in my son's neck to keep him from

01:09:23.166 --> 01:09:27.528
bleeding out. We ain't got no problem with

01:09:28.011 --> 01:09:31.188
setting money aside for the sheriff's department or first responders.

01:09:31.607 --> 01:09:35.041
But That, you know,

01:09:35.137 --> 01:09:38.646
coming at us, you know, hey, we're going to increase taxes 5, 10,

01:09:38.679 --> 01:09:42.430
15%. You know, we can understand

01:09:42.930 --> 01:09:46.612
that. But 220%?

01:09:46.741 --> 01:09:49.556
I'm living off of credit cards.

01:09:51.459 --> 01:09:54.931
I'm sure there's a lot of other families that are doing the same. Fixed incomes,

01:09:56.126 --> 01:09:59.453
single-income household. This is going

01:09:59.953 --> 01:10:02.540
to break me. I won't be able to afford it.

01:10:05.237 --> 01:10:09.070
And we ended up getting kicked out of American Homes

01:10:09.118 --> 01:10:13.000
for Rent because of the incident with my son, even though we

01:10:13.500 --> 01:10:16.756
had no idea, you know, we couldn't prevent that. That was

01:10:17.256 --> 01:10:18.408
an incident that came from a whole other town.

01:10:22.532 --> 01:10:25.644
Yeah, we got kicked out, and by the grace of God, he gave

01:10:26.144 --> 01:10:30.163
us our own home to move into. But now that's about to be taken

01:10:30.663 --> 01:10:32.753
away, and I ain't got nowhere else to go.

01:10:35.359 --> 01:10:39.282
So I hope that y'all don't have your minds already set

01:10:39.782 --> 01:10:43.024
up on approving this, because it's going to put not

01:10:43.073 --> 01:10:45.893
only me and my family, but I'm sure a lot of other families out.

01:10:46.522 --> 01:10:49.245
30 seconds remaining. Thank y'all for listening.

01:10:53.609 --> 01:10:55.454
Mark Cookston. Cookston.

01:11:05.601 --> 01:11:09.418
Good evening, and thank you, uh, City Council and

01:11:09.918 --> 01:11:12.872
everybody that works for the city. This is— I wouldn't want to be in your

01:11:13.372 --> 01:11:16.710
chair. This is going to be very, very difficult for, for you

01:11:16.903 --> 01:11:19.422
as, as it is for for all of us.

01:11:20.991 --> 01:11:24.305
In 2018, I was in the

01:11:24.805 --> 01:11:27.944
hospital for 5 weeks and life-flighted down to the University of Utah. I lost my

01:11:28.444 --> 01:11:31.897
pancreas and automatically became diabetic

01:11:32.869 --> 01:11:36.205
and automatically became tied to Utah.

01:11:36.447 --> 01:11:39.817
We— I was life-flighted down from Idaho,

01:11:40.865 --> 01:11:44.535
and because of that, we have to We

01:11:45.035 --> 01:11:49.065
have to live down here in— or I should say we get to live

01:11:49.179 --> 01:11:53.807
down here in Utah. We chose

01:11:54.467 --> 01:11:58.140
Eagle Mountain because my wife and I grew up in small

01:11:58.994 --> 01:12:02.995
towns in Idaho and liked the small-town values.

01:12:03.820 --> 01:12:06.521
And we saw that in Eagle Mountain.

01:12:07.314 --> 01:12:10.759
We moved in, you know, 5 years ago this coming Thanksgiving.

01:12:11.916 --> 01:12:16.438
And we had just passed 40,000 people here. Now we're

01:12:16.938 --> 01:12:20.567
closing in on 80,000 people. We liked

01:12:20.682 --> 01:12:23.873
the vibe of the community. I will

01:12:23.922 --> 01:12:27.236
say that never in my lifetime did I ever think that I would ever be

01:12:27.318 --> 01:12:30.047
purchasing a home for half a million dollars.

01:12:31.144 --> 01:12:34.486
But coming from Idaho and, you know, coming to

01:12:34.616 --> 01:12:37.438
Utah was an eye-opening experience.

01:12:39.194 --> 01:12:43.105
We chose Eagle Mountain because it was affordable. We were told

01:12:43.605 --> 01:12:47.610
by the previous mayor and then Councilman Gray that,

01:12:48.476 --> 01:12:52.563
oh no, we won't have to raise taxes because we've got large

01:12:52.579 --> 01:12:57.020
companies that are going to be paying a

01:12:58.510 --> 01:13:02.486
large, or footing a large part of

01:13:02.518 --> 01:13:06.148
the taxes down the road. Little did I know that

01:13:06.648 --> 01:13:09.144
down the road is 20 years, long after I'll be dead.

01:13:10.978 --> 01:13:14.772
So that really— that argument was kind of a moot

01:13:14.821 --> 01:13:18.369
point for us. I'm on Social Security.

01:13:19.417 --> 01:13:22.848
Last year I got a raise of $27 a month.

01:13:23.842 --> 01:13:26.927
My God, I thought the rainbow had fallen

01:13:27.427 --> 01:13:27.759
upon my house.

01:13:30.735 --> 01:13:35.234
Then the county of Utah raised

01:13:35.250 --> 01:13:38.633
my taxes $250 last year. 30 seconds remaining. And that was

01:13:38.730 --> 01:13:42.129
all gone. This year we've got

01:13:43.149 --> 01:13:45.951
this one that is proposed. It's going to be wiped out.

01:13:47.274 --> 01:13:50.556
Whatever increase that I, that I get is going to be wiped out.

01:13:52.748 --> 01:13:56.175
What am I supposed to do? Where am I supposed to

01:13:56.192 --> 01:13:58.919
go? This was the most affordable place for us to live.

01:13:59.904 --> 01:14:01.501
I'm here, health reasons, guys.

01:14:03.228 --> 01:14:06.053
Where am I supposed to go? What am I supposed to do?

01:14:06.119 --> 01:14:09.570
Tighten my belt, I was told. Your time is up. Thank you.

01:14:09.619 --> 01:14:10.615
Have you guys tightened your belt?

01:14:19.501 --> 01:14:20.310
Tracy Perretta.

01:14:31.121 --> 01:14:31.379
All righty.

01:14:33.620 --> 01:14:38.813
This isn't

01:14:39.313 --> 01:14:42.736
my first meeting. You all know we've come to these meetings and

01:14:43.236 --> 01:14:46.772
there's been literally nobody here. It's an absolute ghost town. Okay,

01:14:47.418 --> 01:14:50.239
you guys all fit in this City Hall perfectly.

01:14:51.116 --> 01:14:54.365
You don't need this one time you go to raise taxes and we get

01:14:54.381 --> 01:14:58.247
people in here for a meeting. You are fine in

01:14:58.424 --> 01:15:01.735
the building you're in. You don't need to build the new, uh, what do you

01:15:02.235 --> 01:15:04.029
call it, in— it's the new,

01:15:06.997 --> 01:15:10.998
new base camp on the city

01:15:11.030 --> 01:15:14.683
page you did back in March of '25. You put

01:15:15.183 --> 01:15:17.889
up all these plans of everything you guys want to build and spend money on.

01:15:18.610 --> 01:15:21.464
I don't know where you're getting this money, but it shouldn't be from taxes.

01:15:21.528 --> 01:15:25.023
Because I came here and I sat right over there in

01:15:25.523 --> 01:15:28.614
a meeting and I opposed the new data center going in, the QST.

01:15:29.432 --> 01:15:33.087
And I was told by you, Melissa, personally, and Jared, both told

01:15:33.103 --> 01:15:37.078
me afterward, oh, this is such a great thing. The reason we're passing this

01:15:37.608 --> 01:15:40.702
is because our taxes are going to go down. They're going to be so low

01:15:40.958 --> 01:15:44.150
with all the revenue we're going to get from the data centers coming in

01:15:44.727 --> 01:15:48.608
that your taxes are going to go to almost zero. Explain that to

01:15:49.108 --> 01:15:52.537
me personally, Melissa, because I will spend the rest of my time getting you out

01:15:53.037 --> 01:15:56.418
of office because you lied to me. Same for Jared. If,

01:15:56.770 --> 01:16:00.026
if our taxes don't go down to almost zero, why are you

01:16:00.122 --> 01:16:02.784
raising them so high? We don't need a rec center.

01:16:03.409 --> 01:16:06.619
You know, the last thing you need to do is when money is tight is

01:16:06.635 --> 01:16:09.806
say, oh, I need to add on to my house because I get a big

01:16:09.838 --> 01:16:13.654
group of people at Christmas. It's not logical.

01:16:14.427 --> 01:16:17.715
You've got to spend your money wisely. When everybody

01:16:17.747 --> 01:16:21.102
here is tightening their budgets, you guys are building

01:16:21.134 --> 01:16:24.425
new Eagle Mountain city signs because the rocks were

01:16:24.925 --> 01:16:28.339
deteriorating. You know, I left one weekend,

01:16:28.420 --> 01:16:31.940
came back, and I noticed you put up new street signs. What was that price?

01:16:32.005 --> 01:16:35.314
$10,000. Your new street signs that you put up were a

01:16:35.814 --> 01:16:39.286
total of— I mean, the city mount— Eagle Mountain City sign out there

01:16:39.801 --> 01:16:44.252
at Cory Bee Ride, that was probably a $200,000

01:16:44.752 --> 01:16:47.848
project or more. You put in

01:16:48.204 --> 01:16:51.393
a new set of signs that were on that

01:16:52.490 --> 01:16:56.364
page. It says that they were wayfinding sign project to

01:16:56.864 --> 01:16:59.915
have Eagle Mountain and make it more cohesive with their signage.

01:17:00.412 --> 01:17:01.611
And that was $50,000.

01:17:03.547 --> 01:17:07.126
If you tighten your budget everywhere like every single other family has to,

01:17:08.399 --> 01:17:11.608
you could make up the money you need for the police and the

01:17:12.108 --> 01:17:15.965
fire department. 30 seconds remaining. You don't need to take our taxes and

01:17:16.062 --> 01:17:17.725
raise them for something that is just frivolous.

01:17:19.222 --> 01:17:22.923
We don't need a rec center. We don't need a new town city

01:17:23.423 --> 01:17:26.104
hall. Tighten your budget and figure it out.

01:17:26.779 --> 01:17:29.879
'Cause I was told that taxes are going to go down with all the new

01:17:30.379 --> 01:17:32.524
data centers, and that's not what you're doing.

01:17:34.060 --> 01:17:34.301
Thank you.

01:17:38.188 --> 01:17:39.252
Steve Pereda.

01:17:48.125 --> 01:17:50.489
Hi, welcome. Thanks for hearing me.

01:17:52.467 --> 01:17:55.742
My wife just got done speaking about the data centers. I'm going

01:17:55.758 --> 01:17:59.161
to speak about them too. We spoke about them about a year ago.

01:18:00.028 --> 01:18:03.399
We took the math of what the tax revenue was going to be. We divided

01:18:03.899 --> 01:18:07.412
it by the number of households in Eagle Mountain, and we came up with about

01:18:07.477 --> 01:18:11.201
$50 a month towards each household throughout the city of

01:18:11.249 --> 01:18:14.395
Eagle Mountain. So $50 a month

01:18:14.895 --> 01:18:18.971
is $600 a year. Now you're proposing a 220% increase

01:18:19.471 --> 01:18:24.307
that by your own documentation says around $314 a

01:18:24.403 --> 01:18:27.977
year increase. So we have a $900-plus

01:18:28.666 --> 01:18:32.400
differentiation in what your word was a

01:18:32.496 --> 01:18:35.733
year ago because, well, oh, we,

01:18:35.941 --> 01:18:39.531
we need to, we need to allow the data centers. The data centers are good

01:18:39.563 --> 01:18:42.351
because they're going to bring all this tax revenue in and it's going to reduce

01:18:42.851 --> 01:18:46.910
your taxes. A year later were $900 the

01:18:46.942 --> 01:18:50.468
other direction? I'd love to see somebody's math

01:18:50.968 --> 01:18:53.866
on that as to how that math got screwed up.

01:18:55.606 --> 01:18:58.650
So unless you guys fix this— I mean, this was prior to the mayoral race—

01:18:59.826 --> 01:19:02.935
all of these people are— the vast

01:19:02.983 --> 01:19:05.965
majority of these people, I won't say all, are pretty unhappy.

01:19:06.594 --> 01:19:10.207
So when unhappy people go to the voting booths,

01:19:10.830 --> 01:19:12.425
All of you get to go find new jobs.

01:19:13.770 --> 01:19:15.656
Okay?

01:19:20.831 --> 01:19:24.601
If my home budget was short, the first

01:19:25.101 --> 01:19:28.917
thing I'd do as a conservative is I'd figure out how to reduce my spending.

01:19:30.023 --> 01:19:32.584
I don't just go figure out where I can get more money.

01:19:34.195 --> 01:19:37.628
There's also been talk of no transparency. You guys are not giving us

01:19:37.820 --> 01:19:41.112
all of the information. Nope, just trust us.

01:19:41.513 --> 01:19:44.098
But then your stories are changing, so how can we trust you?

01:19:45.542 --> 01:19:49.139
That doesn't work. Inconsistent statements. We need to

01:19:49.155 --> 01:19:53.024
itemize budget. We need to quit spending money like drunken sailors on

01:19:53.524 --> 01:19:56.572
a port call, okay? Um, running out and, and,

01:19:56.684 --> 01:19:59.670
you know, buying signs. Uh, oh,

01:19:59.686 --> 01:20:02.672
let's get a rec center. Let's, let's build a new city hall.

01:20:03.467 --> 01:20:04.052
What's wrong with this one?

01:20:10.206 --> 01:20:14.311
Instead of looking at the entire budget and making educated,

01:20:14.327 --> 01:20:17.410
informed decisions, you guys are taking the easy way out.

01:20:18.282 --> 01:20:21.267
That's the bottom line. Where's the easy money we can get?

01:20:22.381 --> 01:20:26.334
All we have to do is increase our property taxes by 220% and

01:20:26.431 --> 01:20:28.840
we can cover all these other expenses we want to do. Please continue.

01:20:30.244 --> 01:20:34.158
You were elected to make hard decisions. Make those

01:20:34.254 --> 01:20:37.781
hard decisions. Thank you.

01:20:40.288 --> 01:20:40.995
Charlotte Dukos.

01:20:46.735 --> 01:20:50.875
Charlotte Dukos. I'm going to join Jeff

01:20:51.375 --> 01:20:55.063
and Matt in making some comments

01:20:55.563 --> 01:20:58.225
that are maybe a little bit different. I've lived here for 26 years. Years and

01:20:58.306 --> 01:21:00.954
been involved in the city for the majority of that time,

01:21:01.713 --> 01:21:06.202
if not all of it. And over— for

01:21:06.283 --> 01:21:10.093
the last over a year, I've attended almost all city council

01:21:10.593 --> 01:21:12.857
meetings, missed a couple for other things.

01:21:14.400 --> 01:21:17.685
And in attending those meetings, there's a lot of

01:21:18.362 --> 01:21:21.909
the questions that are being presented here tonight that have been answered,

01:21:22.295 --> 01:21:25.426
and I want to acknowledge that. The budget is online,

01:21:26.120 --> 01:21:29.541
line item, in a 200-page document.

01:21:30.639 --> 01:21:33.707
And so that is available. All of these projects,

01:21:33.771 --> 01:21:36.783
everything that we're talking about tonight has been talked about in city meetings. And so

01:21:36.847 --> 01:21:41.041
I want to thank you for actually having those discussions in public meetings

01:21:41.316 --> 01:21:45.295
for those that were there. Eagle Mountain

01:21:45.473 --> 01:21:48.775
has run lean since its beginning. We have employees doing

01:21:48.888 --> 01:21:51.689
the job of 2 to 3 people, probably more in some cases.

01:21:52.793 --> 01:21:55.727
We have offices renting space all over the city because they don't fit in this

01:21:55.823 --> 01:21:59.174
one. We have projects that we have funded but don't

01:21:59.190 --> 01:22:02.861
have personnel to complete, and so they stay undone. We have

01:22:02.893 --> 01:22:06.837
complaints all over the city of things that are not maintained,

01:22:06.885 --> 01:22:09.594
things that have been promised but have not been done,

01:22:10.572 --> 01:22:14.483
and we don't have the personnel to complete it because

01:22:14.515 --> 01:22:18.422
we don't have the money to pay them. And We have

01:22:18.454 --> 01:22:21.719
waited too long to address these shortfalls. They should have been

01:22:21.768 --> 01:22:26.198
addressed years ago in a graduated

01:22:26.247 --> 01:22:29.594
manner, a little at a time, but that did not

01:22:29.627 --> 01:22:32.602
happen. And we can't keep kicking the can down the road.

01:22:32.796 --> 01:22:36.588
At some point, something has to be done, and I applaud you for taking

01:22:37.088 --> 01:22:40.332
the time to do that now. That having been said,

01:22:42.115 --> 01:22:45.409
I do think the communication could probably have improved. I think most

01:22:45.458 --> 01:22:47.506
of you agree with that now as well.

01:22:50.004 --> 01:22:53.234
And I do think that a more moderate

01:22:53.734 --> 01:22:56.865
approach would be good. It's not too late to do that, and I think

01:22:57.365 --> 01:23:00.320
a smaller percentage might be good. I don't think it's going to be a percentage

01:23:00.368 --> 01:23:03.244
that most people like. I still think it needs to be a significant one,

01:23:03.678 --> 01:23:07.262
but maybe not 220. We would go from being

01:23:08.001 --> 01:23:11.440
one of the lowest tax rates in

01:23:11.472 --> 01:23:15.052
the area to the 3rd highest. And I think that maybe something

01:23:15.148 --> 01:23:18.932
a little more moderate would be a good way to start. And maybe we decrease

01:23:19.432 --> 01:23:22.908
that amount a little bit. 30 seconds remaining. I also would encourage

01:23:22.924 --> 01:23:26.211
you to put a policy in place that I do not believe is existing right

01:23:26.711 --> 01:23:30.475
now where we review this yearly or every other year and

01:23:30.975 --> 01:23:34.772
do graduated increases as they are needed. We need to stop being afraid to

01:23:35.590 --> 01:23:38.973
balance our budget on a yearly basis so

01:23:39.473 --> 01:23:42.388
that these big jumps don't have to happen. And that is my— the conclusion of

01:23:42.404 --> 01:23:43.953
my comments. Thank you so much. much for your service.

01:23:47.122 --> 01:23:47.660
Michael Valentini.

01:23:54.594 --> 01:23:57.663
Hello, my name is Michael Valentini.

01:23:58.036 --> 01:24:01.923
I moved out here almost 2 years ago to the date. Um, we moved

01:24:01.971 --> 01:24:05.527
out here because it, uh, gave us an opportunity that

01:24:06.027 --> 01:24:09.431
we didn't have in Lehi for our children. Uh, One thing

01:24:09.463 --> 01:24:13.045
I'd like to say is that the data centers,

01:24:13.736 --> 01:24:17.189
my question for you is what tax breaks did the data centers

01:24:17.689 --> 01:24:21.317
get? So I've been a union member of Local 140 Plumbers and

01:24:21.350 --> 01:24:23.968
Pipefitters here in Utah for 29 years.

01:24:24.723 --> 01:24:28.128
I work at the data centers. I've worked at Facebook and QTS

01:24:28.514 --> 01:24:32.401
since 2000. Okay, that's my question.

01:24:32.899 --> 01:24:36.078
QTS has 3 buildings going on now.

01:24:36.608 --> 01:24:39.707
A 4th is being built now. The 5th is coming.

01:24:40.365 --> 01:24:44.155
From what I understand, there'll be 6 additional buildings at QTS.

01:24:44.540 --> 01:24:47.848
Facebook has 5 buildings now, the 3

01:24:48.348 --> 01:24:51.107
ECO— or the 3 original buildings,

01:24:51.460 --> 01:24:54.559
2 additional buildings that went in just previously,

01:24:54.912 --> 01:24:58.589
and they are building 2 more buildings out there now. So what

01:24:59.089 --> 01:25:02.359
tax breaks do they get? As more people

01:25:02.859 --> 01:25:06.191
come in building these, that brings revenue into the

01:25:06.207 --> 01:25:09.573
economy. Am I wrong to say that there's

01:25:10.073 --> 01:25:13.774
6,000, 4,000 to 6,000 construction workers between Facebook

01:25:14.274 --> 01:25:17.990
and QTS building those facilities? They bring money into this community every day

01:25:18.727 --> 01:25:21.565
at the gas stations, the grocery stores, everything.

01:25:22.110 --> 01:25:25.861
So that generates money for this community.

01:25:26.278 --> 01:25:30.077
Okay, we do need to have police, a police force out here, the first

01:25:30.109 --> 01:25:33.571
responders. Those are very important, but we also need

01:25:33.956 --> 01:25:37.707
to be able to live. There are a lot of communities that are being built

01:25:38.207 --> 01:25:41.458
in here that have, what do they call them, the ADUs, apartments in

01:25:41.554 --> 01:25:45.097
the basements. So that shows that people that are buying these houses

01:25:45.113 --> 01:25:48.623
are supplementing income by having renters in

01:25:49.123 --> 01:25:52.759
their basements. Okay, what's the average income

01:25:52.871 --> 01:25:56.309
of of Eagle Mountain, 78,000? What's the average

01:25:56.809 --> 01:26:00.760
cost of a house? What's the average cost of that house? And then

01:26:01.260 --> 01:26:04.225
you want to increase our taxes by 220%.

01:26:04.436 --> 01:26:08.869
So if we haven't had a tax increase on

01:26:09.047 --> 01:26:12.025
our property tax in 10 or 15 years,

01:26:12.446 --> 01:26:15.153
why wasn't this budgeted in at 5%,

01:26:15.769 --> 01:26:19.157
2% a year over the last 15 years?

01:26:19.986 --> 01:26:23.929
That's kind of piss-poor planning. It really is.

01:26:24.140 --> 01:26:27.673
Sorry to say it. So, 30 seconds remaining. You got it.

01:26:28.091 --> 01:26:31.304
I work 60, 70 hours a week, not because I like

01:26:31.804 --> 01:26:35.160
to, but because I try to provide for my family so that we can have

01:26:35.660 --> 01:26:38.918
the house we live in, the vehicles that we drive, and take vacations,

01:26:38.950 --> 01:26:42.419
put food on our table. When these property taxes go up, and they're

01:26:42.919 --> 01:26:46.376
going to go up on residents and commercial— commercial is going raise their

01:26:46.844 --> 01:26:50.200
cost of living, their prices at the grocery stores,

01:26:50.296 --> 01:26:54.104
at the convenience stores, everywhere. And it's going to affect everybody in

01:26:54.604 --> 01:26:58.021
this room, not just 220%. Your time

01:26:58.070 --> 01:27:01.699
is up. Thank you. Hi, my name is

01:27:02.199 --> 01:27:02.655
Elba Maria Perez.

01:27:12.486 --> 01:27:15.308
And pretty much everything that I was going to say has been said,

01:27:16.574 --> 01:27:19.884
so I don't want to repeat it. The only thing that I have not heard

01:27:19.948 --> 01:27:23.335
is that I don't hope,

01:27:23.974 --> 01:27:27.748
but I pray that you guys really listen

01:27:27.942 --> 01:27:31.110
to what is being said. Each one

01:27:31.610 --> 01:27:35.253
of you, really listen, because people are suffering and

01:27:35.270 --> 01:27:39.270
you're choking us by these big increases

01:27:39.531 --> 01:27:40.899
in taxes.

01:27:43.142 --> 01:27:47.284
I really pray that you will listen to what has been said this evening.

01:27:48.922 --> 01:27:49.212
That's all.

01:27:52.375 --> 01:27:53.165
Walter Peterson.

01:28:00.189 --> 01:28:03.080
Hi, good evening. I'm Walter Peterson. I've lived here for about 3 years,

01:28:03.819 --> 01:28:07.253
uh, and we just were able to buy a home here in Eagle Mountain,

01:28:07.911 --> 01:28:12.068
um, which we're really excited about. I'm a little less excited with the 220%

01:28:12.100 --> 01:28:15.455
increase, um, and a lot of my thoughts

01:28:15.955 --> 01:28:19.836
have been said. Um, a more moderate view

01:28:20.109 --> 01:28:22.805
of this or increase would be appreciated here.

01:28:23.351 --> 01:28:26.529
I'm also extraordinarily wary about the school district

01:28:27.029 --> 01:28:30.801
coming in next year as a teacher That is something that worries me with

01:28:31.301 --> 01:28:34.079
that, where I probably won't have a pay increase for those few years where they're

01:28:34.579 --> 01:28:38.963
trying to get going. And so having

01:28:39.060 --> 01:28:42.434
maybe a 100%, 130%, I don't know,

01:28:42.531 --> 01:28:46.034
a smaller number increase would be greatly appreciated if you

01:28:46.050 --> 01:28:49.826
do have time to make that change. I think

01:28:50.326 --> 01:28:52.783
that you've heard that from the other people that have spoken this evening,

01:28:54.100 --> 01:28:57.608
but We appreciate what you do, and we hope that you listen

01:28:58.043 --> 01:28:59.089
tonight. Thank you.

01:29:02.645 --> 01:29:03.165
Jacob Moore.

01:29:18.271 --> 01:29:21.011
Thank you to the City Council and Mayor Gray. My name is Jacob Moore.

01:29:21.698 --> 01:29:25.355
Not intending to make a comment tonight, and I initially strongly opposed this increase.

01:29:26.780 --> 01:29:30.531
However, I recently received more clear information to the city's purpose

01:29:31.320 --> 01:29:35.280
and why the drastic 221% increase. The state

01:29:35.780 --> 01:29:39.267
is planning on passing a law this next legislative session limiting any city

01:29:39.445 --> 01:29:42.790
to a 5% increase, so Eagle Mountain City has to do it now

01:29:43.501 --> 01:29:47.611
or will be restricted by state policies because Utah's

01:29:47.627 --> 01:29:50.760
revenue Not rate-driven, the massive growth has not

01:29:51.260 --> 01:29:54.693
increased the city's tax revenue because the rate is lowered to account for the growth,

01:29:55.033 --> 01:29:58.926
which keeps the revenue roughly the same. That's something

01:29:59.426 --> 01:30:02.198
that I've frequently heard: that we've had so much growth, we should have more money.

01:30:03.020 --> 01:30:06.083
But that's apparently not the way it works here in Utah.

01:30:07.576 --> 01:30:11.238
It's important to understand that the 221% increase applies only

01:30:11.738 --> 01:30:15.099
to the city's portion of your property tax bill, not your. Total property taxes.

01:30:15.761 --> 01:30:20.229
For the average homeowner, that translates to roughly a 12% increase

01:30:20.729 --> 01:30:23.655
in the overall property tax, not 221%.

01:30:25.208 --> 01:30:28.911
The city wants the property tax increase so our full sheriff's contract is paid for

01:30:29.008 --> 01:30:32.660
by the property taxes— been said multiple times tonight— not having to

01:30:33.160 --> 01:30:36.827
pull those millions from the city's general fund. I've been told that the funds

01:30:36.843 --> 01:30:40.526
freed up— the funds freed up in the general fund would be used for infrastructure

01:30:40.993 --> 01:30:44.230
and other public safety improvements. If that's true,

01:30:44.359 --> 01:30:48.498
then the messaging from the city has not been as misleading

01:30:48.547 --> 01:30:52.252
or dishonest as a lot of people are saying. I believe it would

01:30:52.752 --> 01:30:55.104
go a long way if the city council and mayor would explain as much as

01:30:55.152 --> 01:30:58.229
possible exactly what the freed-up general fund money would be used for,

01:30:59.078 --> 01:31:02.603
as others have requested. I do believe

01:31:03.103 --> 01:31:06.315
it's unfortunate that the city's hand is being forced by the state legislature, which wants

01:31:06.815 --> 01:31:09.371
the step into city policies and tell cities what they are and are not allowed

01:31:09.871 --> 01:31:14.080
to do with their tax rates. I'm not opposed

01:31:14.339 --> 01:31:17.677
anymore, but I believe a smaller increase, as many others have said, is a better

01:31:18.177 --> 01:31:19.977
solution than the proposed increase.

01:31:23.148 --> 01:31:26.859
And I did want to add that

01:31:27.359 --> 01:31:31.101
I encourage Eagle Mountain citizens to ask the state legislature

01:31:31.601 --> 01:31:35.424
to change the property tax to a rate-driven system. So as the population

01:31:35.924 --> 01:31:38.870
increases, our revenue does as well. Instead of the current system,

01:31:39.304 --> 01:31:43.409
it is forcing the city council's hand to increase our taxes to

01:31:43.909 --> 01:31:47.532
increase the revenue. And then I do also believe

01:31:48.032 --> 01:31:51.464
that it's— there's been

01:31:51.640 --> 01:31:55.110
unintentional confusion. 30 seconds remaining. And it's not the

01:31:55.610 --> 01:31:59.673
same as dishonesty as many are claiming tonight. I feel

01:32:00.173 --> 01:32:03.403
like a lot of emotions are clouding judgment. I wanna thank you for all you

01:32:03.903 --> 01:32:06.535
do. I can't imagine being in your shoes, and I'm glad I'm not.

01:32:07.892 --> 01:32:08.507
Have a great night.

01:32:11.933 --> 01:32:15.320
We do have a form filled out by Garrett Houghter, who does not

01:32:15.820 --> 01:32:18.223
want to make a verbal comment, but did note down, I want to echo what

01:32:18.723 --> 01:32:22.435
Charlotte Duco said. And then our next one is Jason Rasmussen.

01:32:33.220 --> 01:32:36.476
Good afternoon. Jason Rasmussen. I've been a resident here for

01:32:36.492 --> 01:32:40.503
3 years. First of all, I want to thank all of you for the

01:32:40.519 --> 01:32:44.225
efforts that you make, and I want to thank our

01:32:45.011 --> 01:32:48.909
public first responders for all the things

01:32:49.166 --> 01:32:51.171
that they do to, to keep our city safe.

01:32:52.310 --> 01:32:56.966
I think A lot of the frustration that we're

01:32:57.046 --> 01:33:00.578
hearing is essentially what you did is you held up a

01:33:01.078 --> 01:33:04.913
marble that said public safety and you put it under a cup

01:33:05.413 --> 01:33:08.092
and then you had 3 other cups. You flipped them around,

01:33:08.847 --> 01:33:12.219
you pulled up the cups, and what you revealed was a card that

01:33:12.719 --> 01:33:14.515
said 210% tax increase.

01:33:15.896 --> 01:33:19.924
And so we're a little bit confused how this public safety marble

01:33:20.424 --> 01:33:23.851
is replaced with a, a 210% or 220%

01:33:24.252 --> 01:33:27.571
tax increase. Um, and I know that a lot of people

01:33:28.071 --> 01:33:32.268
have already expressed, um, that we just need more transparency about,

01:33:33.133 --> 01:33:36.548
like, how the monies would be spent. We need more

01:33:36.596 --> 01:33:40.267
transparency about how money could be reclaimed. We need

01:33:40.767 --> 01:33:44.515
more transparency about how money could be saved.

01:33:44.997 --> 01:33:48.432
How you can retrench in ways. So it's essentially

01:33:48.464 --> 01:33:51.643
just what can you do to kind of let us know how the money is

01:33:51.675 --> 01:33:54.773
going to be spent? Are there other sources of revenue?

01:33:55.126 --> 01:33:58.577
And how can you retrench in places that you can retrench?

01:33:59.284 --> 01:34:01.836
And I would add just one additional item.

01:34:03.072 --> 01:34:06.861
I know that a lot of the data centers that have been built in Eagle

01:34:07.361 --> 01:34:10.922
Mountain have been built with, you know, tax breaks of

01:34:11.422 --> 01:34:15.796
up to 77%. $150 million,

01:34:16.233 --> 01:34:19.776
and that's a large percentage more than the $6

01:34:20.276 --> 01:34:23.498
million revenue that you're trying to get. And it

01:34:23.998 --> 01:34:28.305
seems in some ways like you gave a break to artificial intelligence

01:34:29.098 --> 01:34:33.086
at the expense of all the human intelligences in

01:34:33.134 --> 01:34:36.612
this room and in our community. So thank you.

01:34:36.676 --> 01:34:37.368
Thank you.

01:34:40.529 --> 01:34:41.366
Joy Rasmussen.

01:34:49.969 --> 01:34:53.827
So in 2018, Facebook got

01:34:53.891 --> 01:34:57.941
tax breaks on their property taxes that

01:34:57.989 --> 01:35:01.243
was pretty hefty, and some of you were involved

01:35:01.743 --> 01:35:05.505
in that. It was $150 million. in property tax incentives

01:35:05.602 --> 01:35:09.150
that they are not paying for, what, 40 years? So that's money the

01:35:09.650 --> 01:35:12.410
city could have been using all this time that you took away from us.

01:35:13.469 --> 01:35:18.222
And then 2021, more data centers were given $77

01:35:18.286 --> 01:35:21.273
million in property tax incentives, again for Meta.

01:35:22.140 --> 01:35:25.528
QTS is currently building more data centers that

01:35:26.028 --> 01:35:29.670
are for Meta and Google, and they have also been given tax breaks

01:35:30.184 --> 01:35:34.038
on sales tax. So the city has made a choice. Do we tax

01:35:34.279 --> 01:35:38.116
data centers to build AI to take our jobs and

01:35:38.132 --> 01:35:41.263
take our children's jobs and then tax the residents,

01:35:42.002 --> 01:35:45.197
or do we not do that? And you have made those choices. Now, to say

01:35:45.697 --> 01:35:49.083
that you're paying the price for previous politicians— most of you have been

01:35:49.131 --> 01:35:52.150
here in city politics for many years. You have voted.

01:35:52.503 --> 01:35:55.922
Last year's budget, you did not increase property taxes,

01:35:56.018 --> 01:35:59.500
but you added public safety officers, and you bragged about it on your

01:36:00.000 --> 01:36:03.126
website. I took the screenshot tonight. Somehow you managed to do it before, but now

01:36:03.174 --> 01:36:06.286
you're saying you can't anymore. I have done some research, and guess

01:36:06.786 --> 01:36:10.394
what? When you add data centers to your city, public infrastructure costs

01:36:10.894 --> 01:36:14.212
go up. So somebody in this, in this town, Alex Washburn,

01:36:14.228 --> 01:36:17.934
has done a GRAMA request and asked you guys for information

01:36:18.434 --> 01:36:21.623
about why you're doing this and where you're spending the money and what capital projects

01:36:22.123 --> 01:36:25.486
this is going to go towards, because that's what it's for. And his request was

01:36:25.550 --> 01:36:28.579
denied, and you made him— you're going to charge him a huge fee he can't

01:36:28.595 --> 01:36:32.122
afford. And then you met with him and somehow got him to think it

01:36:32.622 --> 01:36:35.824
was necessary. But here's the thing. We have a lot more houses in Eagle Mountain

01:36:36.324 --> 01:36:38.949
than we did before. So even if the amount that you can charge per house

01:36:38.998 --> 01:36:41.834
has not increased, the number of houses has increased.

01:36:42.059 --> 01:36:44.912
So you still have more revenue with the increase in citizens.

01:36:45.409 --> 01:36:48.470
This is absolutely to fund the data centers. There's an electrician in Eagle Mountain that

01:36:48.970 --> 01:36:52.316
has messaged me. He works at the data centers. He said that QTS wants to

01:36:52.816 --> 01:36:56.947
put 27 data centers in Eagle Mountain. There's already about 7 approved.

01:36:57.828 --> 01:37:01.257
And that's— he said if he lived here, he would be upset.

01:37:01.850 --> 01:37:04.638
He said he's not going to stay because the energy costs and the water costs

01:37:05.138 --> 01:37:08.147
are going to skyrocket. He doesn't understand why the residents are not upset. The city

01:37:08.163 --> 01:37:11.592
has been trying to put nuclear reactors in the city for the data centers.

01:37:12.089 --> 01:37:14.509
All of you in this room need to know this and wake up. We need

01:37:15.009 --> 01:37:17.475
to fight this like Box Elder County. Thank you. because we are already paying the

01:37:17.975 --> 01:37:21.761
price. These data centers are getting the break and we're getting dorked over. 30 seconds

01:37:21.809 --> 01:37:25.533
remaining. People can't afford it. There's a lady I know who messaged

01:37:25.581 --> 01:37:29.112
me. She is elderly. Her husband has dementia and Parkinson's.

01:37:29.497 --> 01:37:32.563
They are on fixed incomes. And she said, our house is paid for, but we

01:37:33.063 --> 01:37:36.399
cannot afford this property tax increase. My husband's gonna have to go into a

01:37:36.899 --> 01:37:40.444
care center for $5,000 a month. This is going to bankrupt us. You need

01:37:40.492 --> 01:37:43.750
to think about those people and not do this. This is totally inappropriate. There needs

01:37:44.250 --> 01:37:46.970
to be more time. and more public disclosure about where this money is really going

01:37:47.082 --> 01:37:51.095
and what infrastructure you're putting it towards, what capital projects, and give— listen

01:37:51.128 --> 01:37:54.270
to the people. Your time is up. Thank you.

01:37:56.268 --> 01:37:56.976
Michael Carey.

01:38:05.145 --> 01:38:08.384
Michael Carey. I'm going to read this. Mayor and members of

01:38:08.884 --> 01:38:11.964
the City Council, thank you for your service and for the opportunity to speak tonight.

01:38:12.773 --> 01:38:16.427
I want to begin by saying that I support public safety. I believe our deputies

01:38:16.603 --> 01:38:20.914
and first responders deserve the resources they need to protect our growing community.

01:38:21.571 --> 01:38:25.498
As Eagle Mountain continues to grow, it is reasonable to expect that the cost

01:38:25.998 --> 01:38:29.857
of providing those services will grow as well. My concern is not whether we

01:38:30.002 --> 01:38:33.287
should invest in public safety. My concern is the size of the proposed

01:38:33.787 --> 01:38:36.733
increase and whether residents have been given the complete financial picture.

01:38:37.518 --> 01:38:41.589
The city's public information states that every dollar of the proposed increase will go toward

01:38:41.670 --> 01:38:44.991
funding the sheriff's contract and expanding public safety. At the same

01:38:45.491 --> 01:38:49.228
time, the city's public— published materials also discuss other financial

01:38:49.728 --> 01:38:52.598
pressures facing Eagle Mountain, including rapid population growth,

01:38:52.614 --> 01:38:56.418
inflation, increased road maintenance, parks infrastructure, and other essential

01:38:56.610 --> 01:39:00.189
city services. If public safety is the immediate

01:39:00.221 --> 01:39:03.816
use of these new tax dollars, I understand that. But if broader budget

01:39:03.848 --> 01:39:07.491
pressure— pressures are also contributing to the need for

01:39:07.539 --> 01:39:11.292
this increase, I believe residents deserve a transparent discussion about

01:39:11.792 --> 01:39:15.734
those challenges as well. An informed public is better able to support difficult

01:39:15.799 --> 01:39:19.696
decisions. I would also encourage the City Council to consider a phased approach

01:39:19.808 --> 01:39:23.095
instead of implementing the full increase in a single year.

01:39:24.041 --> 01:39:27.201
A 3 to 5 year graduated plan would still provide additional

01:39:27.701 --> 01:39:31.595
funding for public safety while giving families time to adjust to higher property

01:39:32.095 --> 01:39:35.493
taxes during a period when many are already experiencing

01:39:35.589 --> 01:39:38.705
rising costs in housing, insurance, groceries,

01:39:38.962 --> 01:39:43.281
and utilities. A 3 to 5— sorry,

01:39:43.458 --> 01:39:46.605
a phased approach would also allow the city to measure results along the way.

01:39:47.087 --> 01:39:50.925
Before each phase, the City Council could publicly report measurable

01:39:51.425 --> 01:39:54.201
outcomes such as improvements in emergency response times,

01:39:54.618 --> 01:39:58.537
changes in deputy workload and staffing ratios, growth in calls

01:39:58.569 --> 01:40:01.989
for service, progress toward clearly defined public safety goals,

01:40:02.423 --> 01:40:06.326
Whether growth-related revenues or operational efficiencies have reduced

01:40:06.358 --> 01:40:10.422
the need for future tax increases. I would also respectfully

01:40:10.454 --> 01:40:14.229
ask the council to explain why 7 additional deputies represent

01:40:14.729 --> 01:40:17.956
the appropriate staffing level and what objective analysis supports that

01:40:18.004 --> 01:40:21.923
recommendation. Understanding the data behind the proposal will help public

01:40:22.180 --> 01:40:25.987
confidence. Finally, I encourage the council to continue exploring

01:40:26.180 --> 01:40:29.648
every available option to reduce the burden on taxpayers,

01:40:30.088 --> 01:40:32.797
including efficiencies within city operations,

01:40:33.370 --> 01:40:37.258
careful prioritization of spending, and identifying growth-related

01:40:37.758 --> 01:40:41.292
revenue sources before asking residents to absorb significant

01:40:41.792 --> 01:40:45.332
increases in property taxes. Please conclude. I believe Eagle Mountain residents are willing to invest

01:40:45.832 --> 01:40:48.594
in their community when they understand the need and have confidence in the plan.

01:40:48.787 --> 01:40:52.290
Transparent, measurable, and great— a gradual approach can strengthen

01:40:52.790 --> 01:40:55.947
that trust while still meeting city's responsibilities, keep our community safe.

01:40:56.385 --> 01:40:59.208
Thank you for your time and service and for your consideration.

01:41:02.132 --> 01:41:02.881
Camille Gardner.

01:41:09.386 --> 01:41:13.623
I don't see Camille. We'll add her paper to the record.

01:41:14.610 --> 01:41:17.891
Please remember you represent those who elected you. We don't need additional police,

01:41:17.908 --> 01:41:21.796
nor all the other projects you think we do. We want economy at

01:41:22.296 --> 01:41:26.151
the city. Like Stuart Adams, we will vote you out if

01:41:26.651 --> 01:41:30.362
you vote for this increase. Additionally, we don't need Ranches Parkway widened. We need

01:41:30.623 --> 01:41:31.505
a right-hand turn lane.

01:41:35.340 --> 01:41:36.189
KB Bergenson.

01:41:45.943 --> 01:41:48.876
Good evening. K.B. Bergeson. I've lived here about 3 years.

01:41:49.870 --> 01:41:53.638
Before that, I lived in California and Washington, and I moved here to get away

01:41:53.702 --> 01:41:58.719
from those places, so I was glad to be here. But I

01:41:58.847 --> 01:42:02.935
am a 7-year Army veteran, and I also retired

01:42:03.435 --> 01:42:05.532
from law enforcement. I worked for a sheriff's office.

01:42:06.606 --> 01:42:10.390
So I have deep respect and am grateful for the services they

01:42:10.890 --> 01:42:14.001
do provide us. Thank you. And I'm grateful, you know,

01:42:14.017 --> 01:42:16.488
for their service and what they, you know, do for us.

01:42:17.700 --> 01:42:21.755
I'm 75 years old, and I live with my daughter

01:42:21.836 --> 01:42:24.927
and her family. I came here to join with them

01:42:25.427 --> 01:42:28.526
so we could be on a budget and survive the economy.

01:42:28.574 --> 01:42:32.432
I'm on a fixed budget. I'm retired. With that

01:42:32.932 --> 01:42:36.624
in mind, I don't think that we need a 220% increase

01:42:37.124 --> 01:42:40.347
in property tax. to support

01:42:40.847 --> 01:42:44.776
law enforcement and what they're doing. I emailed

01:42:45.195 --> 01:42:47.419
all of you, you know, asking you about this,

01:42:48.337 --> 01:42:52.157
and I did receive one response from Craig, and I appreciate that.

01:42:52.399 --> 01:42:55.915
I thought it was very insightful. I quote, he said,

01:42:56.091 --> 01:42:59.337
also, I don't think we need— that we'll end up

01:42:59.837 --> 01:43:03.049
needing a 220% increase. In the past few weeks, we've been diving into

01:43:03.097 --> 01:43:06.617
the numbers, and I think the city can get by with a small smaller number

01:43:07.117 --> 01:43:10.247
than 220%. I'm not sure what number. It will still be a

01:43:10.747 --> 01:43:14.455
large increase, but not 220%. A few comments I'll give you since

01:43:14.551 --> 01:43:17.989
I've been on the council for 3.5 years. We anticipate—

01:43:18.358 --> 01:43:22.133
next year we anticipate revenue— that data

01:43:22.633 --> 01:43:25.939
center revenues will take a jump. We need an increase to help with additional needs.

01:43:26.630 --> 01:43:29.874
If next year doesn't bring enough data center revenue, I'm sure 3 and 4 years

01:43:29.906 --> 01:43:33.424
we'll see that money coming in. Further, we should have

01:43:33.924 --> 01:43:36.871
Smith development online by then as well, and I think there's a realistic possibility to

01:43:37.371 --> 01:43:40.863
revisit that increase. I think if that's the case,

01:43:40.959 --> 01:43:44.646
if that's in mind, we should take a measured approach to any increase right

01:43:45.146 --> 01:43:48.509
now. There's other things that can be done for law enforcement, too. I know

01:43:48.590 --> 01:43:52.373
that there's other places I've been, they've had a citizens patrol where

01:43:52.873 --> 01:43:56.332
they have seniors volunteer to take a workload off of deputies.

01:43:56.829 --> 01:43:59.634
That can be done, and maybe that can be looked into. There's a lot of

01:44:00.134 --> 01:44:03.746
other things that be done and looked into to help with law enforcement without,

01:44:03.891 --> 01:44:07.426
you know, budgeting huge amounts of money. I'm on a fixed

01:44:07.926 --> 01:44:11.459
balanced budget, and I think that the city should also be on a fixed balanced

01:44:11.959 --> 01:44:15.074
budget. You need to take the funds that you make and use

01:44:15.574 --> 01:44:19.428
them wisely and determine what takes priority and spend that money— 30 seconds remaining.

01:44:19.493 --> 01:44:22.851
—according to those priorities, and other things should not be done until the money

01:44:23.351 --> 01:44:26.128
comes in and it can be spent accordingly. Thank you very much.

01:44:28.700 --> 01:44:29.347
Steve Campbell.

01:44:35.192 --> 01:44:37.340
Mayor Gray, councilmen, Councilman Wright,

01:44:38.324 --> 01:44:41.419
I'm a 20-year resident. I'm going to make this really simple.

01:44:41.548 --> 01:44:44.451
I think we've been here long enough and everyone has said a lot, but I

01:44:44.951 --> 01:44:48.814
have a question. The other day I just happened to hear that

01:44:49.314 --> 01:44:54.386
the federal government Office of Management and Budget

01:44:54.886 --> 01:44:58.181
provides grants to cities. A grant is free money. I mean,

01:44:58.197 --> 01:45:01.759
it's not free, it's our tax dollars to the federal government.

01:45:02.455 --> 01:45:06.101
They will provide grants to cities to upgrade

01:45:06.343 --> 01:45:09.731
public safety, police departments, this type

01:45:10.231 --> 01:45:13.803
of thing. I wasn't aware of this. I don't know if you folks are

01:45:13.852 --> 01:45:17.626
aware or not. If you're not, it bears

01:45:17.723 --> 01:45:21.305
looking into. Yes. If you have, great.

01:45:21.871 --> 01:45:25.319
I don't know the process for applying for

01:45:25.351 --> 01:45:28.820
a grant. I do know they're available. My daughter gets

01:45:29.320 --> 01:45:32.539
them all the time from the federal government for disadvantaged children in the

01:45:33.039 --> 01:45:36.568
school systems. So just point of interest.

01:45:36.714 --> 01:45:39.106
Anyway, good to see you, Brett. Good to see you all. Thank you very much.

01:45:43.951 --> 01:45:45.284
Shedrick D. Shermond.

01:45:48.441 --> 01:45:51.164
Feel free to correct me if I'm not close. Okay. Yeah,

01:45:54.080 --> 01:45:57.555
for the record, Cedric DeChermond. Um, I was going to write this with the help

01:45:58.055 --> 01:46:01.239
of AI, but the Wi-Fi wouldn't connect, and I thought maybe it's a little too

01:46:01.739 --> 01:46:03.250
ironic to not just speak from the heart.

01:46:05.404 --> 01:46:07.898
So my wife and I moved to Eagle Mountain a little over 3 years ago

01:46:08.157 --> 01:46:11.007
due to the prospect of affordable living, safety,

01:46:11.740 --> 01:46:14.146
well-planned growth strategy, and to raise our own family.

01:46:15.792 --> 01:46:19.269
I've worked and lived all across this country. This is the first home I've ever

01:46:19.769 --> 01:46:23.553
bought, and I'm proud of it. As a young family, our budget is tight,

01:46:23.634 --> 01:46:26.308
and our options are weighed when we spend our hard-earned money.

01:46:27.118 --> 01:46:29.889
We want to start a family and often deliberate how.

01:46:31.298 --> 01:46:34.260
I won't explain what it is you're doing in economic principles.

01:46:34.936 --> 01:46:38.373
Plenty of us have already done that already, and frankly, should already know.

01:46:38.870 --> 01:46:42.189
Taxes and costs often go up and rarely go down.

01:46:42.702 --> 01:46:46.486
I worry that you already know that too. The proposed tax

01:46:46.986 --> 01:46:50.671
increase, or upon its original inception, does not even begin to address

01:46:50.783 --> 01:46:54.198
concerns regarding the following: future impacts due to the new school

01:46:54.246 --> 01:46:57.469
district— and my wife is a teacher— um, current shortfalls

01:46:57.533 --> 01:47:01.670
in infrastructure and future growth of infrastructure needs. The irony

01:47:01.766 --> 01:47:05.149
in the truth and transparency is that as taxpayers, we are

01:47:05.649 --> 01:47:08.989
seeing a limited view you into the current stewardship of the use of our current

01:47:09.489 --> 01:47:13.539
tax revenue. If you are a poor steward now, you will be a worse steward

01:47:13.651 --> 01:47:16.720
with more. But as a general populace,

01:47:16.866 --> 01:47:20.391
we cannot contend with what we do not know and what you are failing to

01:47:20.407 --> 01:47:23.884
accurately disclose. We as citizens can't keep up with all of

01:47:24.384 --> 01:47:28.455
the wavering of priorities and promises being potentially broken. We can nonetheless see

01:47:28.955 --> 01:47:32.843
that you are ostensibly lying. Are all of the

01:47:33.343 --> 01:47:36.850
developers, outside contractors, and multibillion-dollar industries that operate

01:47:37.350 --> 01:47:40.937
and profit off of our city paying their fair share? We all know the answer.

01:47:41.482 --> 01:47:44.174
You want to hold our feet to the fire but won't stand against them.

01:47:44.767 --> 01:47:48.438
Can you account for the impact of this proposed tax increase in terms of

01:47:48.774 --> 01:47:52.797
hungry mouths, missed payments, and ultimately families no longer

01:47:53.297 --> 01:47:55.890
being able to call Eagle Mountain their home? I don't think you can.

01:47:57.268 --> 01:48:00.426
You can't share the budget you have, and you can't show the forecast for the

01:48:00.926 --> 01:48:04.466
projects you want. A lot of people blame young kids for the hoodrat behavior

01:48:04.562 --> 01:48:07.433
and damage we see growing around here. I blame parenting.

01:48:07.946 --> 01:48:11.057
Can we account for the lack of parental guidance as a result of them

01:48:11.557 --> 01:48:14.793
having to work harder to pay for this fund? Are we operating

01:48:14.841 --> 01:48:18.256
in a banana republic? I and others helped elect you in those chairs

01:48:18.529 --> 01:48:22.474
on the principles of family values, economic frugality, and fiscal conservatism.

01:48:22.939 --> 01:48:26.050
Is this tyranny? We have enough of that going on in our country and in

01:48:26.550 --> 01:48:29.997
our world. This shitty council should reject those ends. I would

01:48:30.497 --> 01:48:33.772
request that you consider a motion to defer this vote until you can better communicate

01:48:34.272 --> 01:48:37.919
your past decisions, future, future intents, and your clearly stated budget

01:48:38.419 --> 01:48:41.829
objectives to the community that deserves to hear a transparent truth of the situation.

01:48:42.734 --> 01:48:43.009
Thank you.

01:48:46.130 --> 01:48:46.776
Isaac Gardner.

01:48:51.526 --> 01:48:54.540
He did provide a written comment in opposition to the tax increase.

01:48:54.704 --> 01:48:59.032
We will add it to the For the record, Daniel Lamb— Lob.

01:49:00.164 --> 01:49:04.109
Feel

01:49:04.125 --> 01:49:08.099
free to correct me if I'm incorrect on your name. For some reason

01:49:08.276 --> 01:49:09.967
it's always Lamb. It's Lob.

01:49:10.837 --> 01:49:14.589
Anyway, thank you for having this opportunity for

01:49:14.621 --> 01:49:18.114
us to speak. I'm here not because I want to be, like a

01:49:18.614 --> 01:49:20.304
lot of other people. We have a lot of other things we want to be

01:49:20.804 --> 01:49:24.512
doing. But we're so against this increase, that's why we're here.

01:49:24.641 --> 01:49:26.777
We can't, we don't feel that we can afford this.

01:49:28.127 --> 01:49:31.473
Transparency has been discussed. Like, I just agree with all the other comments that

01:49:31.973 --> 01:49:33.718
have been made. Like, that's probably the best way to sum it up.

01:49:36.200 --> 01:49:39.870
Yeah, right now we're not buying it. We're just, we don't buy what

01:49:40.370 --> 01:49:43.058
you guys are proposing. We don't agree to it. That's why I'm here is to,

01:49:43.450 --> 01:49:45.964
you know, make my voice heard. Don't agree to it.

01:49:47.688 --> 01:49:50.961
There's—it's not the best thing,

01:49:51.153 --> 01:49:54.859
and I hate to say this. Like I'm not trying to be offensive, but the

01:49:55.359 --> 01:49:58.469
citizens, like for myself, I will try to make sure you're not

01:49:58.969 --> 01:50:02.559
reelected again. I will. If this passes, just know it

01:50:03.059 --> 01:50:07.051
may be your last term. So anyway, we appreciate everything else you're

01:50:07.551 --> 01:50:11.174
doing that's that's positive, and not trying to be negative here, but we

01:50:11.206 --> 01:50:14.844
really don't want this increase. And if it goes through and

01:50:15.344 --> 01:50:17.690
you pass it, it's a death knell. Pretty sure about that.

01:50:22.920 --> 01:50:23.606
Shawna Clark.

01:50:26.727 --> 01:50:29.700
Is that right? Shawna?

01:50:29.893 --> 01:50:31.002
Okay.

01:50:35.808 --> 01:50:39.391
I wasn't going to get up today because I'm not very eloquent and there's

01:50:39.891 --> 01:50:41.158
been a lot of people that have talked very well.

01:50:43.158 --> 01:50:45.962
But the more I sat there, the more I just wanted to make sure that

01:50:46.699 --> 01:50:49.984
I'm just not a person sitting in the audience observing, that you know how

01:50:50.484 --> 01:50:54.343
I feel. In September of 1998, my family moved out here.

01:50:55.048 --> 01:50:58.477
So next month will be 28 years that I've been out here. We moved

01:50:58.977 --> 01:51:02.948
out here because we couldn't afford to live anywhere else. I raised

01:51:03.448 --> 01:51:06.073
my kids out here. I became single out here through divorce.

01:51:06.730 --> 01:51:10.257
And I've been able to stay here. Thank you. My youngest daughter and

01:51:10.757 --> 01:51:14.420
her 4 kids, age range in age from 3

01:51:14.550 --> 01:51:17.843
to 9, live with me as well. She stays

01:51:17.875 --> 01:51:21.279
home to take care of the kids, and I make $16 an hour.

01:51:29.468 --> 01:51:31.147
I've heard it said about the impact fees.

01:51:34.125 --> 01:51:37.467
The homes being built, more money that

01:51:37.516 --> 01:51:41.569
way. I just feel like with the

01:51:41.698 --> 01:51:45.873
tax breaks that other big businesses get and then

01:51:46.067 --> 01:51:49.609
being scammed out of the money, I feel like me as a $16

01:51:50.109 --> 01:51:53.753
an hour person am being asked to pay that. It is not

01:51:54.253 --> 01:51:57.799
my fault. Not that it's your fault, not all

01:51:57.847 --> 01:52:01.263
of it. But I feel like this is a huge

01:52:02.203 --> 01:52:05.363
ask of you guys. Not ask, you're not asking us, you're just gonna do it.

01:52:07.529 --> 01:52:11.101
I've had to refinance my house a few times to get my ex-husband

01:52:11.166 --> 01:52:14.592
off, to get money out because I couldn't afford

01:52:14.657 --> 01:52:18.715
things. And the last time was to lower

01:52:18.763 --> 01:52:22.034
my interest rate. So even though I've been out here for almost 28 years,

01:52:22.549 --> 01:52:26.177
I still owe 25 years on my house. It's not like I

01:52:26.274 --> 01:52:30.046
can save many other places. So I really wish

01:52:30.095 --> 01:52:33.774
you would think about how this affects the small people.

01:52:37.880 --> 01:52:38.603
Dax Steadily.

01:52:43.311 --> 01:52:46.926
I do not see him present. Also in opposition to the tax increase.

01:52:46.991 --> 01:52:49.802
We will add his comment to the record. Colton Hart.

01:52:55.664 --> 01:52:58.678
I do not see him in opposition to the tax increase.

01:52:59.493 --> 01:53:01.983
We'll add his comment to the record. Sadie Hart,

01:53:07.528 --> 01:53:10.744
also opposition to the tax increase.

01:53:10.858 --> 01:53:12.210
We'll get that one added as well.

01:53:13.992 --> 01:53:15.110
Melissa Gordette.

01:53:20.487 --> 01:53:23.585
She states, please don't raise our taxes. I do not see her in person.

01:53:23.634 --> 01:53:26.971
We'll add her comment to the record. Kristen Meyer.

01:53:37.873 --> 01:53:41.679
Good evening, Mayor and City Council members. My name is Kristen Meyer and

01:53:42.179 --> 01:53:45.570
I'm a resident of Eagle Mountain. I'm here tonight to urge you to vote no

01:53:46.070 --> 01:53:48.734
on the proposed tax increase. Let me state why.

01:53:49.761 --> 01:53:54.209
Roughly $1.5 million is allocated to the Utah County Sheriff's contract.

01:53:54.787 --> 01:53:58.303
I don't have an issue with that. My issue is

01:53:58.335 --> 01:54:02.157
with the remaining amount that has been— it hasn't been

01:54:02.173 --> 01:54:05.304
allocated clearly enough. We wanna know

01:54:05.804 --> 01:54:08.258
exactly how it will be spent. Thank you.

01:54:10.458 --> 01:54:14.569
These are public funds and we need transparency, not vague line items.

01:54:14.890 --> 01:54:18.374
Second, how did we get here? The podcast indicated

01:54:18.406 --> 01:54:22.950
that a failed bill from the previous legislative session may have capped— it

01:54:22.982 --> 01:54:26.595
might have capped future tax increases. Fair enough.

01:54:27.237 --> 01:54:30.433
But your response, along with other cities, seems to be that we should

01:54:30.933 --> 01:54:33.885
raise taxes now before the state can cap us in the future.

01:54:34.466 --> 01:54:37.945
And the bill failed. And what is the response? As a

01:54:38.445 --> 01:54:41.270
city, you knew we were growing. You approved the development.

01:54:41.820 --> 01:54:45.428
You approved the growth. And instead of having the common sense to plan

01:54:45.444 --> 01:54:49.035
for the roads and the infrastructure and all the needs that we require,

01:54:49.181 --> 01:54:50.160
you failed to act.

01:54:54.010 --> 01:54:57.793
Third, we are in an affordability crisis. It's a crisis

01:54:57.906 --> 01:55:01.385
fueled in part by greedy corporations. And the politicians who

01:55:01.885 --> 01:55:05.330
too often put the powerful interests ahead of the hardworking Americans.

01:55:06.758 --> 01:55:10.175
I propose you lower the tax to cover only the sheriff's contract.

01:55:11.009 --> 01:55:13.543
And before these words fall on deaf ears,

01:55:14.201 --> 01:55:18.163
think about the people you represent. Think about the senior living

01:55:18.371 --> 01:55:21.515
on a fixed income. Think about the mother wondering how she's going to

01:55:22.015 --> 01:55:25.413
make it to the next paycheck. Think about the people who have experienced the

01:55:25.429 --> 01:55:27.947
embarrassment of having their credit card declined.

01:55:29.489 --> 01:55:33.127
Although we do not have the power to decide how you vote,

01:55:33.610 --> 01:55:36.894
we do have the power to decide who votes in these seats tomorrow.

01:55:40.158 --> 01:55:43.856
And I ask that you earn our trust. Vote no on this proposal

01:55:44.356 --> 01:55:47.636
as it stands, and we ask for greater transparency.

01:55:48.220 --> 01:55:48.416
Thank you.

01:55:52.572 --> 01:55:53.358
Cheryl Carr.

01:56:04.644 --> 01:56:06.959
Good evening. My name is Cheryl Carr.

01:56:09.945 --> 01:56:12.589
We bought our land in 1998.

01:56:13.572 --> 01:56:15.781
We built our home in 2004.

01:56:16.152 --> 01:56:19.961
Been here for 22 years. I'm 71

01:56:19.994 --> 01:56:23.373
years old. Thank you. My husband is 76.

01:56:28.241 --> 01:56:31.441
Our property has more than doubled

01:56:31.811 --> 01:56:35.781
since we've been here. Our income has

01:56:35.894 --> 01:56:40.170
not. That value is not realized

01:56:40.558 --> 01:56:44.134
unless we sell our home. I want to

01:56:44.634 --> 01:56:48.327
read President Donald Trump

01:56:50.097 --> 01:56:52.962
has— he may be federal, but this is his view.

01:56:54.032 --> 01:56:57.777
He has proposed eliminating local property taxes for homeowners

01:56:58.918 --> 01:57:02.872
aged 65 and older who have fully paid off

01:57:03.372 --> 01:57:06.665
their mortgages. He characterized property taxes as a

01:57:06.713 --> 01:57:10.393
form of perpetual rent that prevents seniors on

01:57:10.506 --> 01:57:14.121
fixed incomes from From truly owning their own homes.

01:57:16.110 --> 01:57:20.016
Relief for fixed incomes— supporters state the plan protects

01:57:20.097 --> 01:57:23.825
older Americans from raising housing insurance and

01:57:23.890 --> 01:57:27.691
valuation costs. Aging in place— advocates

01:57:27.789 --> 01:57:31.817
argue it helps retirees keep their lifelong homes

01:57:32.319 --> 01:57:36.131
instead of being forced to move. I will tell you,

01:57:36.874 --> 01:57:40.837
if this passes, we will have to sell and we

01:57:41.337 --> 01:57:41.701
will have to move.

01:57:47.208 --> 01:57:49.389
I know there needs to be more money.

01:57:52.297 --> 01:57:58.117
And the people who are coming to Eagle Mountain create

01:57:58.744 --> 01:58:00.741
more traffic on the roads. We've all seen that.

01:58:01.829 --> 01:58:05.376
So what is the answer? What would you like to see happen?

01:58:06.441 --> 01:58:10.216
It's, it's a tough one, but I think that the impact fees

01:58:10.394 --> 01:58:15.128
need to be raised. I don't know what they are, but I do know that

01:58:15.385 --> 01:58:18.743
this problem is a result of

01:58:18.792 --> 01:58:22.326
more people moving here, and they

01:58:22.826 --> 01:58:24.563
need to pay for that impact.

01:58:25.754 --> 01:58:29.519
And so that would be my request.

01:58:30.119 --> 01:58:34.379
That you look at those impact fees and see where things

01:58:34.476 --> 01:58:37.122
can be shifted. 30 seconds remaining.

01:58:38.526 --> 01:58:41.748
I do thank you for your service and for your time. Thank you.

01:58:44.211 --> 01:58:44.826
Roger Laird.

01:58:54.386 --> 01:58:58.066
Sorry, I'm not exactly Just as nice as everybody, but my

01:58:58.195 --> 01:59:02.221
day started at 2:30 this morning, and I didn't

01:59:02.721 --> 01:59:05.891
get off until 4:30 today, and I rushed down

01:59:06.108 --> 01:59:07.678
to be here for this.

01:59:09.809 --> 01:59:11.896
220% is rather asinine.

01:59:14.096 --> 01:59:18.254
I probably more than anybody in here support police

01:59:18.302 --> 01:59:22.358
officers and EMS because I spent the entirety of my young adulthood

01:59:22.858 --> 01:59:26.421
in EMS. I've been shot at. I've been stabbed.

01:59:27.137 --> 01:59:29.628
I've been shoulder to shoulder with police fighting.

01:59:31.861 --> 01:59:37.211
And it's not fun. Well, it was, but— But

01:59:37.824 --> 01:59:41.342
probably none of you guys have been shot at or stabbed or been in

01:59:41.374 --> 01:59:44.909
those situations or watched people die or drug a

01:59:45.409 --> 01:59:48.845
wounded police officer that was shot because some gangbanger wanted

01:59:48.861 --> 01:59:51.397
some clout while we were on the side of a road at a call.

01:59:53.531 --> 01:59:57.022
I work very hard for my money. We moved here because

01:59:57.522 --> 02:00:00.949
it was affordable, it was a nice community, and it's a little bit a ways

02:00:01.046 --> 02:00:04.822
from it all. You can't

02:00:05.322 --> 02:00:10.076
tell me, you can't convince me 220% is

02:00:10.659 --> 02:00:14.028
reasonable. Some of you are real estate agents. That is

02:00:14.528 --> 02:00:17.957
a negative at asset that you're trying to sell people.

02:00:19.403 --> 02:00:22.905
And if you're the kind of real estate agent that sells negative assets

02:00:23.018 --> 02:00:26.553
to people, I would probably say you're not exactly an ethical

02:00:27.053 --> 02:00:30.347
real estate agent. I did real estate, one of the many things I've

02:00:30.847 --> 02:00:34.155
done, besides EMS paramedic, crane operator,

02:00:34.941 --> 02:00:37.985
real estate, and mortgage loan officer.

02:00:39.590 --> 02:00:43.070
So, The fact that you guys

02:00:43.182 --> 02:00:46.605
can't articulate where all that's going other than you're selling it under

02:00:46.621 --> 02:00:50.092
the guise of helping the police officers, which is a good thing. I don't

02:00:50.592 --> 02:00:54.652
think anybody's opposed to giving them help and the EMS any

02:00:54.684 --> 02:00:58.331
help. But those

02:00:58.428 --> 02:01:01.900
data centers, which I've worked on, I've been on a crane in there for 16

02:01:02.013 --> 02:01:05.564
hours one day. The fact,

02:01:05.666 --> 02:01:06.743
and it's you,

02:01:08.789 --> 02:01:12.399
Oh, the tax breaks you give them could be paying for all of

02:01:12.899 --> 02:01:16.008
this. And, and the, the bullcrap part is you guys

02:01:16.073 --> 02:01:19.512
know it, but you give them all these tax breaks.

02:01:19.560 --> 02:01:22.974
And then all these builders that want to come in, and we're getting more revenue

02:01:23.071 --> 02:01:26.840
from taxes on that. Again, you know it. I'm not saying

02:01:26.937 --> 02:01:30.577
you guys— that things weren't mismanaged in the past, but you can fix

02:01:31.077 --> 02:01:34.617
it by simply cutting costs and stop giving all these tax

02:01:35.117 --> 02:01:38.537
breaks. There's 7 more buildings going in there. I know that because

02:01:38.602 --> 02:01:41.243
I work there. Please do better.

02:01:44.267 --> 02:01:46.735
Budget like we all do.

02:01:48.587 --> 02:01:48.928
Thank you.

02:01:52.406 --> 02:01:54.456
Zeke, Zeke Magdalio.

02:02:01.407 --> 02:02:04.043
Hi, my name is Zeke Magdaleno. I've been here about 7 years.

02:02:04.493 --> 02:02:08.093
I'm kind of neutral, gentleman right here, uh,

02:02:08.173 --> 02:02:12.402
between the data centers and a resident because I build them and

02:02:12.902 --> 02:02:15.955
I know what they cost. I know what they bring in, and I have to

02:02:16.455 --> 02:02:17.715
be careful what I say so I have a job tomorrow.

02:02:18.970 --> 02:02:22.609
So, but I, I'm finding

02:02:23.109 --> 02:02:27.452
myself not understanding Because I feel it's a duty to—

02:02:28.093 --> 02:02:30.901
even though I could lose my job if I'm not careful,

02:02:31.462 --> 02:02:34.238
I have to say something for all these people here,

02:02:35.168 --> 02:02:38.681
including myself, that might not be able to afford a

02:02:38.697 --> 02:02:41.072
home. I was able to, as a single dad,

02:02:42.371 --> 02:02:45.868
afford a house on a single income,

02:02:46.061 --> 02:02:49.590
raise my children, and I'll be perfectly honest, I hated it

02:02:49.767 --> 02:02:52.985
in the middle of the desert. I couldn't stand it. But we've come

02:02:53.035 --> 02:02:56.602
a long way in 6 years. So I want

02:02:57.102 --> 02:03:02.480
to bring some transparency for the people behind me on

02:03:02.512 --> 02:03:06.597
the data centers. And by

02:03:07.097 --> 02:03:10.679
the time QTS is done— I can say QTS, we all know it's signs out

02:03:11.179 --> 02:03:15.028
there— they're predicted that Eagle Mountain will be the biggest

02:03:15.229 --> 02:03:19.234
data center campuses for them in the world.

02:03:20.105 --> 02:03:22.554
Not United States, the world.

02:03:24.134 --> 02:03:28.095
Let that sink in. So if

02:03:28.595 --> 02:03:32.296
we're allowing these data centers to be built and we get— we are getting them

02:03:32.344 --> 02:03:35.933
tax breaks, which I understand, we want them to come here

02:03:35.981 --> 02:03:39.288
and build these data centers, but isn't that supposed to help these

02:03:39.402 --> 02:03:42.709
people, us, out in the long run? That's what I thought.

02:03:42.806 --> 02:03:46.588
That's what they're supposed to do. And I know how many they're planning on building.

02:03:47.718 --> 02:03:51.218
Honestly, we shouldn't have to pay taxes for our lifetime.

02:03:51.828 --> 02:03:55.183
These guys have so much money. I know what they bring in when they rent

02:03:55.683 --> 02:03:59.101
these data centers, and it's insane.

02:03:59.695 --> 02:04:02.793
It's insane how much money that, that these,

02:04:03.949 --> 02:04:07.529
these people have that are building these data centers. So I'm

02:04:07.626 --> 02:04:12.426
confused on why 220%

02:04:13.662 --> 02:04:16.930
Why are we paying anything? I, I maybe I got here late,

02:04:16.946 --> 02:04:19.799
so I'm sorry if this was talked about earlier.

02:04:20.696 --> 02:04:24.109
But being that I'm building them and I'm kind of neutral,

02:04:25.182 --> 02:04:28.900
I just don't see— and I'm, I, you know, obviously I'm a community

02:04:29.400 --> 02:04:33.033
member paying my mortgage. That's insane. I think that comes

02:04:33.533 --> 02:04:36.591
out to like $300 more, I think, a month, something like that.

02:04:37.039 --> 02:04:40.741
That's crazy. But anyways, just to stick up for the data centers a

02:04:40.805 --> 02:04:44.422
little bit, The ones we're building are closed systems. They don't use water

02:04:44.697 --> 02:04:48.013
like the other ones, just letting you know. They do in the beginning, but they're

02:04:48.513 --> 02:04:51.496
closed. They're not evaporative. That's Facebook.

02:04:51.724 --> 02:04:53.753
I worked on that one too. That's all I gotta say.

02:04:59.670 --> 02:05:00.449
Megan Streeter.

02:05:08.338 --> 02:05:10.470
Does it start when I speak? Hi,

02:05:11.063 --> 02:05:14.542
I'm a delegate and precinct chair in Eagle

02:05:15.042 --> 02:05:17.459
Mountain and have interacted with several of my city council members.

02:05:18.052 --> 02:05:21.323
Nice to see you, Brett. Nice to see you, Melissa. I know you two and

02:05:21.339 --> 02:05:24.641
find you to be reasonable, logical humans. And with that said, I do feel like

02:05:24.689 --> 02:05:27.526
we are missing a mark here. I do feel that way,

02:05:28.392 --> 02:05:30.989
especially with the sheriffs. I do not dislike the sheriffs,

02:05:31.694 --> 02:05:35.573
appreciate you, but I do think in the current state we're in, I mean,

02:05:35.766 --> 02:05:38.074
I think it's a good idea to invest with them in the current state we're

02:05:38.574 --> 02:05:40.153
in, but I do feel that we need our own department.

02:05:42.757 --> 02:05:45.077
And with that said,

02:05:47.446 --> 02:05:50.637
renting is worse than owning, and I do feel like we are making

02:05:50.733 --> 02:05:54.090
a bad decision by renting the sheriffs. I don't think it's an

02:05:54.590 --> 02:05:58.035
investment for our city. Aside from that, I do believe we are missing the opportunity

02:05:58.535 --> 02:06:01.239
to negotiate with data centers, and he pretty much set me up for success when

02:06:01.271 --> 02:06:04.639
he was speaking. I have a unique perspective as I have rented

02:06:05.139 --> 02:06:08.182
land from many of the farmers out there by the data centers. I have

02:06:08.214 --> 02:06:11.391
watched as these farmers have been cornered. I've watched as they have been

02:06:11.423 --> 02:06:15.160
bullied. I've watched even their own cows

02:06:15.433 --> 02:06:19.026
be poisoned. And we're not— I mean, there's so many stories you

02:06:19.526 --> 02:06:21.224
guys don't know about, and you haven't been out there talking to the farmers.

02:06:21.272 --> 02:06:25.106
And if you've ignored them, then you would know what's been going on.

02:06:26.084 --> 02:06:29.886
One of those guys out there, he leased his land for $100,000 a

02:06:30.386 --> 02:06:33.977
month. And then when he's done leasing, he will be bought out.

02:06:35.885 --> 02:06:39.653
And then just one QTS manager gets

02:06:40.153 --> 02:06:43.581
$500,000 for 10 months. We need to stop acting like we need the data

02:06:44.081 --> 02:06:46.676
centers and start acting like they need us, as they do. We have the land

02:06:46.708 --> 02:06:50.316
and the water to provide space for them. Data centers are being banned all over

02:06:50.816 --> 02:06:53.779
the nation and in the world, and we know this. It's a hot topic right

02:06:54.279 --> 02:06:57.916
now. They need us, period. And they have the money to give us

02:06:58.416 --> 02:07:01.780
the full $7 million you need for the 220 increase. I guarantee that

02:07:02.280 --> 02:07:05.050
you can negotiate that. Thank you. I have faith in you. I absolutely believe that

02:07:05.550 --> 02:07:09.154
you guys could do this because they need us. Eagle Mountain's special. We're unique.

02:07:09.940 --> 02:07:13.547
And aside from that, I love this city, and I hope we can

02:07:14.047 --> 02:07:17.939
manage these situations in a way that allows us to move forward in

02:07:18.276 --> 02:07:21.739
a small-town ideal since a lot of these people moved here for that,

02:07:21.803 --> 02:07:25.506
and I did as well. And I absolutely hate your job. I'm sure it's horrible,

02:07:25.650 --> 02:07:27.943
but I really think that we're missing the mark, and I really hope we can

02:07:28.443 --> 02:07:30.149
do better. Thank you. do something better. I really do.

02:07:33.573 --> 02:07:35.735
Tony Castillo.

02:07:45.429 --> 02:07:49.061
Tony Castillo. You know, everybody knows

02:07:49.093 --> 02:07:52.391
who we are. We own a roofing company. COVID hit us hard.

02:07:54.740 --> 02:07:58.407
I saw prices go up every month, my material cost

02:07:58.698 --> 02:08:01.153
every month, 10% here, 10% there.

02:08:02.496 --> 02:08:04.543
I'd go to my wife, we gotta raise our prices.

02:08:06.790 --> 02:08:10.684
And this is after my suppliers were chewing me out because they

02:08:11.184 --> 02:08:13.410
were hearing from competitors how I was undercutting them.

02:08:15.287 --> 02:08:18.700
And I said, is it affecting your bottom line? I'm still buying

02:08:18.749 --> 02:08:22.392
from you guys. The only difference is I'm not getting rich like those

02:08:27.450 --> 02:08:30.610
This year, I'm not talking COVID, we had about a 60% price increase.

02:08:32.400 --> 02:08:34.440
60% just in one year.

02:08:36.868 --> 02:08:40.089
And I got smart, didn't change suppliers,

02:08:41.966 --> 02:08:42.662
just negotiated.

02:08:45.961 --> 02:08:49.464
This year we had about a 30% price increase because of the war.

02:08:53.060 --> 02:08:56.387
I watched my— I'm going to use this to be upfront, guys. My per bundle

02:08:56.887 --> 02:09:00.904
price to operate my company for

02:09:01.032 --> 02:09:04.340
one brand is $150 a bundle.

02:09:05.147 --> 02:09:08.765
That was after the price increase that I got. And I went

02:09:08.797 --> 02:09:10.234
back and I said, I can't operate like this.

02:09:15.110 --> 02:09:18.165
And, you know, a lot of you guys are my customers.

02:09:19.250 --> 02:09:22.421
I had Charlotte ask me, her daughter asked me, how the heck are you $5,000

02:09:22.566 --> 02:09:25.592
less than these other companies, but you're doing more?

02:09:26.846 --> 02:09:29.410
I want your business. I know my numbers.

02:09:31.000 --> 02:09:33.645
I'll go back to my suppliers and renegotiate.

02:09:35.290 --> 02:09:38.814
You guys get to renegotiate. Yeah. I support the tax increase.

02:09:42.849 --> 02:09:45.229
220%— I mean, I'll be honest with you, it's very shocking.

02:09:47.456 --> 02:09:49.758
Can you imagine if I raised my prices 220%?

02:09:51.730 --> 02:09:55.462
I mean, Craig, you had a customer beat me up over

02:09:55.962 --> 02:09:59.178
the quote I gave him, even a repair. I had to walk

02:09:59.678 --> 02:10:03.310
away from it. Had I done it, it would have opened me into a multimillion-dollar

02:10:03.810 --> 02:10:07.309
community. Thank you. But my values are a lot worth more than that.

02:10:10.579 --> 02:10:11.791
Elections are coming up again.

02:10:16.110 --> 02:10:19.787
At the end of the day, guys, do what's right. 30 seconds remaining. A lot

02:10:20.287 --> 02:10:23.561
of us can't afford to eat. And I was like,

02:10:25.346 --> 02:10:28.460
I'm wondering, you know, can I afford to buy a cow this year

02:10:29.138 --> 02:10:32.512
if the rate goes up? 'Cause that's the first thing I'm gonna be cutting.

02:10:33.144 --> 02:10:37.209
So thanks, guys. Appreciate y'all.

02:10:38.893 --> 02:10:42.921
I have Melanie Castillo who chooses not to make a verbal comment. And while she

02:10:42.953 --> 02:10:46.577
states, while I support an increase and see its need, she's interested

02:10:47.077 --> 02:10:50.708
to hear from each member of the council the top 3 capital projects. And she's

02:10:51.208 --> 02:10:54.438
seen the list and wants to know what's important to the

02:10:54.938 --> 02:10:58.228
council members on that one. And then we do have,

02:10:58.244 --> 02:11:02.189
we did have a public comment from Matthew Joseph who has

02:11:02.302 --> 02:11:05.034
that he would like to discuss the budget. And we just wanna remind you that

02:11:05.534 --> 02:11:08.504
this is for the proposed tax rate only, that the budget public hearing will be

02:11:08.521 --> 02:11:12.585
on August 18th. So if Matthew Joseph wanted to clarify

02:11:12.940 --> 02:11:16.104
that, and I don't see him here, so we will add it to

02:11:16.604 --> 02:11:20.000
the record. Joanna Brown.

02:11:27.798 --> 02:11:32.326
Hi, Joanna Brown. I'm sorry that I'm dressed this way. I would

02:11:32.826 --> 02:11:36.405
never approach in any other circumstance, but I heard a comment that

